window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-07-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2"]={"id":"CGL-07-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2","title":"CGL 07 OCT 2026 SHIFT 2","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000073981","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Find the 3<sup>rd</sup> letter to the left of the letter equidistant from C and O. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"C तथा O से समान दूरी पर स्थित अक्षर के बाईं ओर 3<sup>रा</sup> अक्षर ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"H"},"2":{"en":"F"},"3":{"en":"G"},"4":{"en":"J"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Alphabet positions: C = 3 and O = 15.<br>The letter equidistant from both is the middle one: \\(\\frac{3 + 15}{2}\\) = 9, that is I.<br>3rd letter to the left of I: H, G, F → F<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): F.</b>","hi":"वर्णमाला क्रमांक: C = 3 तथा O = 15।<br>दोनों से समान दूरी पर स्थित अक्षर मध्य वाला है: \\(\\frac{3 + 15}{2}\\) = 9, अर्थात् I।<br>I से तीसरा अक्षर बाईं ओर: H, G, F → F<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): F है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000073982","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A man walks at 5 km/h and runs at 10 km/h. He covers a distance in 2 hours, walking half the time and running the other half. What is the total distance? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति 5 किमी/घंटा की चाल से चलता है तथा 10 किमी/घंटा की चाल से दौड़ता है। वह 2 घंटे में दूरी तय करता है, जिसमें आधा समय चलता है और आधा दौड़ता है। कुल दूरी क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12.5 km","hi":"12.5 किमी"},"2":{"en":"15 km","hi":"15 किमी"},"3":{"en":"18.5 km","hi":"18.5 किमी"},"4":{"en":"7.5 km","hi":"7.5 किमी"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Time is split equally, so walking time = 1 hour and running time = 1 hour.<br>Distance walked = 5 × 1 = 5 km<br>Distance run = 10 × 1 = 10 km<br>Total distance = 5 + 10 = <b>15 km</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 15 km.</b>","hi":"समय बराबर बँटा है, अतः चलने का समय = 1 घंटा तथा दौड़ने का समय = 1 घंटा।<br>चलकर तय दूरी = 5 × 1 = 5 किमी<br>दौड़कर तय दूरी = 10 × 1 = 10 किमी<br>कुल दूरी = 5 + 10 = <b>15 किमी</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 15 किमी है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000073983","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What is the 5<sup>th</sup> term of<br>3, 6, 12, 24 ...? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"3, 6, 12, 24 ... का 5<sup>वाँ</sup> पद क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"40"},"2":{"en":"42"},"3":{"en":"48"},"4":{"en":"50"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Each term is double the term before it: 3 × 2 = 6, 6 × 2 = 12, 12 × 2 = 24.<br>5<sup>th</sup> term = 24 × 2 = <b>48</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 48.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद अपने पिछले पद से दोगुना है: 3 × 2 = 6, 6 × 2 = 12, 12 × 2 = 24।<br>5<sup>वाँ</sup> पद = 24 × 2 = <b>48</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 48 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000073984","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"The average of 5 numbers is 12. If one of these numbers is replaced by 20, the new average becomes 14. What was the original number that was replaced? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"5 संख्याओं का औसत 12 है। यदि इनमें से एक संख्या को 20 से बदल दिया जाए, तो नया औसत 14 हो जाता है। बदली गई मूल संख्या क्या थी? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4"},"2":{"en":"6"},"3":{"en":"8"},"4":{"en":"10"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Original sum = 5 × 12 = 60<br>New sum = 5 × 14 = 70<br>Increase in the sum = 70 − 60 = 10<br>New number − old number = 10 → 20 − old number = 10 → old number = <b>10</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 10.</b>","hi":"मूल योग = 5 × 12 = 60<br>नया योग = 5 × 14 = 70<br>योग में वृद्धि = 70 − 60 = 10<br>नई संख्या − पुरानी संख्या = 10 → 20 − पुरानी संख्या = 10 → पुरानी संख्या = <b>10</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 10 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000073985","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"<b>Carefully examine the address below and identify which of the following alternatives matches the given address.</b><br>Mr. R. Patel<br>7652 Silver Oak, 7<sup>th</sup> Floor, Ambli Road<br>Ahmedabad, Gujarat - 380058<br><b>Alternatives:</b><br>A) Mr. R. Patel, 7652 Silver Oak, 7th Floor, Ambli Road, Ahmedabad, Gujarat - 380058<br>B) Mr. R. Patel, 7652 Silver Oak, 6th Floor, Ambli Road, Ahmedabad, Gujarat - 380058<br>C) Mr. R. Patel, 7652 Silver Oak, 7th Floor, Ambli Road, Ahmedabad, Gujarat - 380058<br>D) Mr. R. Patel, 7652 Silver Oak, 7th Floor, Ambli Road, Ahmedabad, Gujarat - 380059 [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"<b>नीचे दिए गए पते को ध्यानपूर्वक देखिए और पहचानिए कि निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विकल्प दिए गए पते से मेल खाता है।</b><br>Mr. R. Patel<br>7652 Silver Oak, 7<sup>th</sup> Floor, Ambli Road<br>Ahmedabad, Gujarat - 380058<br><b>विकल्प:</b><br>A) Mr. R. Patel, 7652 Silver Oak, 7th Floor, Ambli Road, Ahmedabad, Gujarat - 380058<br>B) Mr. R. Patel, 7652 Silver Oak, 6th Floor, Ambli Road, Ahmedabad, Gujarat - 380058<br>C) Mr. R. Patel, 7652 Silver Oak, 7th Floor, Ambli Road, Ahmedabad, Gujarat - 380058<br>D) Mr. R. Patel, 7652 Silver Oak, 7th Floor, Ambli Road, Ahmedabad, Gujarat - 380059 [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A and B","hi":"A तथा B"},"2":{"en":"A and C","hi":"A तथा C"},"3":{"en":"B and D","hi":"B तथा D"},"4":{"en":"D and C","hi":"D तथा C"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Given address: Mr. R. Patel, 7652 Silver Oak, 7<sup>th</sup> Floor, Ambli Road, Ahmedabad, Gujarat - 380058.<br>A) 7th Floor and PIN 380058 — matches on every point.<br>B) 6th Floor — the floor is different.<br>C) 7th Floor and PIN 380058 — matches on every point.<br>D) PIN 380059 — the PIN is different.<br>So A and C are identical with the given address.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): A and C.</b>","hi":"दिया गया पता: Mr. R. Patel, 7652 Silver Oak, 7<sup>th</sup> Floor, Ambli Road, Ahmedabad, Gujarat - 380058।<br>A) 7th Floor तथा पिन 380058 — हर बिंदु पर मेल।<br>B) 6th Floor — मंजिल भिन्न है।<br>C) 7th Floor तथा पिन 380058 — हर बिंदु पर मेल।<br>D) पिन 380059 — पिन भिन्न है।<br>अतः A तथा C दिए गए पते से पूरी तरह मेल खाते हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): A तथा C है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000073986","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"TIGER\" is written as \"REGIT.\" How will \"MOUSE\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"TIGER\" को \"REGIT.\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"MOUSE\" को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"ESUOM"},"2":{"en":"MUOSE"},"3":{"en":"OSEUM"},"4":{"en":"MUESO"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"TIGER → REGIT: the letters are written in the reverse order (R, E, G, I, T).<br>MOUSE reversed: E, S, U, O, M → <b>ESUOM</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ESUOM.</b>","hi":"TIGER → REGIT: अक्षर उल्टे क्रम में लिखे गए हैं (R, E, G, I, T)।<br>MOUSE को उल्टा लिखने पर: E, S, U, O, M → <b>ESUOM</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ESUOM है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000073987","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A sum of money becomes ₹ 18,720 in 3 years and ₹ 22,880 in 5 years at simple interest. What is the rate of interest per annum if the principal is ₹ 12,480? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कोई धनराशि साधारण ब्याज पर 3 वर्षों में ₹ 18,720 तथा 5 वर्षों में ₹ 22,880 हो जाती है। यदि मूलधन ₹ 12,480 है, तो प्रति वर्ष ब्याज दर क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(14\\frac{2}{3}\\%\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(16\\frac{2}{3}\\%\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(15\\frac{5}{9}\\%\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(18\\frac{1}{4}\\%\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Interest of 2 years = 22,880 − 18,720 = ₹ 4,160<br>Interest of 1 year = ₹ 2,080<br>Rate = \\(\\frac{2080}{12480}\\) × 100 = 16.67% = \\(16\\frac{2}{3}\\%\\)<br>Check: \\(\\frac{12480 \\times 16\\frac{2}{3} \\times 3}{100}\\) = ₹ 6,240, and 12,480 + 6,240 = 18,720 ✔<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(16\\frac{2}{3}\\%\\).</b>","hi":"2 वर्षों का ब्याज = 22,880 − 18,720 = ₹ 4,160<br>1 वर्ष का ब्याज = ₹ 2,080<br>दर = \\(\\frac{2080}{12480}\\) × 100 = 16.67% = \\(16\\frac{2}{3}\\%\\)<br>जाँच: \\(\\frac{12480 \\times 16\\frac{2}{3} \\times 3}{100}\\) = ₹ 6,240, तथा 12,480 + 6,240 = 18,720 ✔<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(16\\frac{2}{3}\\%\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000073988","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"If ‘A # B’ denotes A is the brother of B, ‘A @ B’ denotes A is the mother of B, ‘A &amp; B’ denotes A is the father of B, and ‘A % B’ denotes A is the sister of B, choose the expression that correctly represents that M is the paternal uncle of N. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि ‘A # B’ का अर्थ है A, B का भाई है, ‘A @ B’ का अर्थ है A, B की माता है, ‘A &amp; B’ का अर्थ है A, B का पिता है तथा ‘A % B’ का अर्थ है A, B की बहन है, तो वह व्यंजक चुनिए जो सही रूप से दर्शाता है कि M, N का ताऊ/चाचा है। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"M # R &amp; N"},"2":{"en":"M % R @ N"},"3":{"en":"M &amp; R # N"},"4":{"en":"M @ R # N"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"134\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 134\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"108\" y=\"34\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"162\" y=\"88\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M172 54V76M172 76V88M122 24H172M122 24V34M172 24V34\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"122\" y=\"48\">M+</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"48\">R+</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"102\">N</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"129\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></svg><br>M # R &amp; N: M is the brother of R, and R is the father of N, so M is N's paternal uncle.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): M # R &amp; N.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"134\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 134\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"108\" y=\"34\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"162\" y=\"88\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M172 54V76M172 76V88M122 24H172M122 24V34M172 24V34\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"122\" y=\"48\">M+</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"48\">R+</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"102\">N</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"129\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ पुरुष  − स्त्री  — भाई-बहन  = पति-पत्नी  | पीढ़ी</text></svg><br>M # R &amp; N: M, R का भाई है तथा R, N का पिता है, अतः M, N का चाचा है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): M # R &amp; N है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000073989","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Candidates appearing from the \"Northern Zone\" are assigned roll numbers starting with 9201. Which of the following roll numbers belongs to a candidate NOT from the Northern Zone? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"\"Northern Zone\" से आने वाले अभ्यर्थियों को 9201 से आरंभ होने वाले रोल नंबर दिए जाते हैं। निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा रोल नंबर उस अभ्यर्थी का है जो Northern Zone का नहीं है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"92014498211"},"2":{"en":"92014498214"},"3":{"en":"92104498217"},"4":{"en":"92014498220"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Roll numbers of the Northern Zone begin with 9201.<br>92014498211, 92014498214 and 92014498220 all begin with 9201.<br>92104498217 begins with 9210, so it cannot belong to the Northern Zone.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 92104498217.</b>","hi":"Northern Zone के रोल नंबर 9201 से आरंभ होते हैं।<br>92014498211, 92014498214 तथा 92014498220 — तीनों 9201 से आरंभ होते हैं।<br>92104498217, 9210 से आरंभ होता है, अतः यह Northern Zone का नहीं हो सकता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 92104498217 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000073990","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Within a mixed team of both new and experienced employees, the experienced members tend to dominate discussions, while a new joiner appears overwhelmed and hesitant to contribute their own ideas. What is the most effective approach to foster inclusivity and improve team participation? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"नए तथा अनुभवी कर्मचारियों की मिश्रित टीम में अनुभवी सदस्य चर्चाओं पर हावी रहते हैं, जबकि एक नया सदस्य अभिभूत तथा अपने विचार रखने में संकोची प्रतीत होता है। समावेशिता बढ़ाने तथा टीम की भागीदारी सुधारने का सबसे प्रभावी उपाय क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Actively ask for the new joiner's opinion in discussions and make space for them to contribute.","hi":"चर्चाओं में नए सदस्य की राय सक्रिय रूप से पूछें और उन्हें योगदान देने का अवसर दें।"},"2":{"en":"Choose to assign critical tasks exclusively to the experienced employees to maintain current workflow.","hi":"वर्तमान कार्यप्रवाह बनाए रखने के लिए महत्वपूर्ण कार्य केवल अनुभवी कर्मचारियों को सौंपें।"},"3":{"en":"Ignore the current situation, as it is considered a natural and expected part of team dynamics.","hi":"वर्तमान स्थिति को अनदेखा करें, क्योंकि इसे टीम गतिशीलता का स्वाभाविक और अपेक्षित हिस्सा माना जाता है।"},"4":{"en":"Politely advise the new joiner to continue observing the team dynamics quietly and learning for now.","hi":"नए सदस्य को विनम्रता से सलाह दें कि वे अभी चुपचाप टीम की गतिशीलता देखते रहें और सीखते रहें।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The new joiner's hesitation comes from being crowded out by the experienced members, not from a lack of ideas.<br>Inviting the opinion directly and creating space for it removes that barrier and uses the whole team's talent.<br>Giving all important work to the experienced members, ignoring the situation, or asking the new joiner to stay quiet keeps the imbalance.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Actively ask for the new joiner's opinion in discussions and make space for them to contribute.</b>","hi":"नए सदस्य का संकोच अनुभवी सदस्यों के दबदबे के कारण है, विचारों की कमी के कारण नहीं।<br>सीधे राय पूछकर और उसके लिए स्थान बनाकर यह अवरोध हटता है और पूरी टीम की क्षमता का उपयोग होता है।<br>महत्वपूर्ण कार्य केवल अनुभवियों को देना, स्थिति को अनदेखा करना या नए सदस्य को चुप रहने की सलाह देना — ये असंतुलन बनाए रखते हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): चर्चाओं में नए सदस्य की राय सक्रिय रूप से पूछें और उन्हें योगदान देने का अवसर दें।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000073991","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"You and two friends are on a train with tickets under RAC (Reservation Against Cancellation). The ticket inspector offers to upgrade you to three full berths in exchange for a bribe. What would be the most ethical and professional way to respond to this situation? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"आप और आपके दो मित्र रेल में यात्रा कर रहे हैं और आपके टिकट RAC (Reservation Against Cancellation) के अंतर्गत हैं। टिकट निरीक्षक घूस के बदले आपको तीन पूर्ण बर्थ देने का प्रस्ताव करता है। इस स्थिति में सबसे नैतिक और व्यावसायिक प्रतिक्रिया क्या होगी? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Agree to pay the requested bribe to the ticket checker, justifying the action because you believe that having a full berth is necessary for a long journey.","hi":"टिकट निरीक्षक को मांगी गई घूस देने पर सहमत हो जाएँ, यह तर्क देकर कि लंबी यात्रा के लिए पूर्ण बर्थ आवश्यक है।"},"2":{"en":"Firmly refuse to pay the bribe and continue to travel by sitting comfortably in your originally allotted seats as per the terms of your current ticket status.","hi":"घूस देने से दृढ़ता से इंकार करें और अपने वर्तमान टिकट की शर्तों के अनुसार आवंटित स्थानों पर आराम से यात्रा जारी रखें।"},"3":{"en":"Forcibly occupy the berths by threatening the current legal occupants, regardless of the potential for physical conflict or the resulting disturbance to other passengers.","hi":"वर्तमान वैध यात्रियों को धमकाकर जबरन बर्थ पर कब्जा कर लें, चाहे शारीरिक टकराव की संभावना हो या अन्य यात्रियों को असुविधा हो।"},"4":{"en":"Utilize your personal connections by calling a friend who is an officer in the railways to pressure the ticket checker into providing you with berths without payment.","hi":"अपने व्यक्तिगत संपर्कों का उपयोग करते हुए रेलवे के अधिकारी मित्र को बुलाकर टिकट निरीक्षक पर दबाव डालें कि वह बिना भुगतान बर्थ दे दे।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A bribe is an illegal payment, and accepting the offer would make you a party to corruption.<br>Refusing firmly and travelling on the seats allowed by the RAC ticket keeps the journey legal and sets the right example for the friends travelling with you.<br>Paying, threatening other passengers or using influence are all improper.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Firmly refuse to pay the bribe and continue to travel by sitting comfortably in your originally allotted seats as per the terms of your current ticket status.</b>","hi":"घूस एक अवैध भुगतान है और प्रस्ताव स्वीकार करने से आप भी भ्रष्टाचार के भागीदार बन जाएँगे।<br>दृढ़ता से इंकार करके RAC टिकट से मिलने वाले स्थानों पर यात्रा करना कानूनी रहता है और साथ चल रहे मित्रों के लिए सही उदाहरण भी बनता है।<br>घूस देना, अन्य यात्रियों को धमकाना या प्रभाव का प्रयोग करना — सभी अनुचित हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): घूस देने से दृढ़ता से इंकार करें और अपने वर्तमान टिकट की शर्तों के अनुसार आवंटित स्थानों पर आराम से यात्रा जारी रखें।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000073992","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"<b>Choose the option which is exactly similar to:</b> Secretary, Lions Club International, Sector 29, Gurgaon-122002 [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"<b>वह विकल्प चुनिए जो ठीक इसके समान है:</b> Secretary, Lions Club International, Sector 29, Gurgaon-122002 [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Secretary, Lions Club International, Sector 29, Gurgaon 122002"},"2":{"en":"Secretary, Lions Club International, Sector 29, Gurgaon-122002"},"3":{"en":"Secretary, Lions Club International, Sector 28, Gurgaon-122002"},"4":{"en":"Secretary, Lions Club International, Sector 29, Gurgaon-122003"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The given address reads: Secretary, Lions Club International, Sector 29, Gurgaon-122002 — with a hyphen before the PIN.<br>Option (1) drops the hyphen, option (3) changes the sector to 28 and option (4) changes the PIN to 122003.<br>Only option (2) reproduces every part of the address exactly.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Secretary, Lions Club International, Sector 29, Gurgaon-122002.</b>","hi":"दिया गया पता है: Secretary, Lions Club International, Sector 29, Gurgaon-122002 — पिन से पहले योजक चिह्न के साथ।<br>विकल्प (1) में योजक चिह्न हट जाता है, विकल्प (3) में सेक्टर 28 हो जाता है और विकल्प (4) में पिन 122003 हो जाता है।<br>केवल विकल्प (2) में पते का प्रत्येक भाग ठीक वैसा ही है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): Secretary, Lions Club International, Sector 29, Gurgaon-122002 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000073993","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"What should come in place of question mark (?) in the following analogy?<br><br>AZB : YCX :: DWE : ? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित सादृश्य में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर क्या आएगा?<br><br>AZB : YCX :: DWE : ? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"BZA"},"2":{"en":"ZBA"},"3":{"en":"YAX"},"4":{"en":"ABC"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"AZB → YCX: A − 2 = Y, Z + 3 = C, B − 4 = X<br>The pattern is −2, +3, −4.<br>DWE: D − 2 = B, W + 3 = Z, E − 4 = A → <b>BZA</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): BZA.</b>","hi":"AZB → YCX: A − 2 = Y, Z + 3 = C, B − 4 = X<br>पैटर्न है −2, +3, −4।<br>DWE: D − 2 = B, W + 3 = Z, E − 4 = A → <b>BZA</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): BZA है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000073994","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the given question, a few statements have been given followed by conclusions based on them. Consider the statements to be true and answer which of the given conclusions logically follow the statement.<br><b>Statements</b><br>1. All satellites are engineered objects.<br>2. Some engineered objects are sustainable.<br>3. No unsustainable object receives certification.<br><b>Conclusions</b><br>I. Some satellites may be sustainable.<br>II. Some engineered objects do not receive certification.<br>III. All satellites receive certification.<br>IV. Some sustainable objects receive certification. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिए गए प्रश्न में कुछ कथन दिए गए हैं, जिनके बाद उन पर आधारित निष्कर्ष हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानिए और उत्तर दीजिए कि दिए गए निष्कर्षों में से कौन-सा तार्किक रूप से कथन का अनुसरण करता है।<br><b>कथन</b><br>1. सभी उपग्रह इंजीनियरित वस्तुएँ हैं।<br>2. कुछ इंजीनियरित वस्तुएँ टिकाऊ हैं।<br>3. कोई भी अटिकाऊ वस्तु प्रमाणन प्राप्त नहीं करती।<br><b>निष्कर्ष</b><br>I. कुछ उपग्रह टिकाऊ हो सकते हैं।<br>II. कुछ इंजीनियरित वस्तुएँ प्रमाणन प्राप्त नहीं करतीं।<br>III. सभी उपग्रह प्रमाणन प्राप्त करते हैं।<br>IV. कुछ टिकाऊ वस्तुएँ प्रमाणन प्राप्त करती हैं। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I and II follow","hi":"केवल I और II निकलते हैं"},"2":{"en":"Only I follows","hi":"केवल I निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Only II and IV follow","hi":"केवल II और IV निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Only I, II and IV follow","hi":"केवल I, II और IV निकलते हैं"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Satellites are engineered objects and some engineered objects are sustainable, so a satellite can be one of those sustainable objects — Conclusion I is only a possibility and hence follows.<br>Conclusion II would need some engineered object that is unsustainable, which the statements do not give, so it does not follow.<br>Nothing links satellites with certification, so Conclusion III does not follow, and IV cannot be drawn from “some engineered objects are sustainable”.<br>Hence only Conclusion I follows.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only I follows.</b>","hi":"उपग्रह इंजीनियरित वस्तुएँ हैं और कुछ इंजीनियरित वस्तुएँ टिकाऊ हैं, अतः कोई उपग्रह उन टिकाऊ वस्तुओं में से हो सकता है — निष्कर्ष I केवल एक संभावना है, इसलिए निकलता है।<br>निष्कर्ष II के लिए ऐसी इंजीनियरित वस्तु चाहिए जो अटिकाऊ हो, जो कथनों से नहीं मिलता, अतः यह नहीं निकलता।<br>उपग्रहों का प्रमाणन से कोई संबंध नहीं दिया गया, अतः निष्कर्ष III नहीं निकलता, और “कुछ इंजीनियरित वस्तुएँ टिकाऊ हैं” से IV नहीं निकाला जा सकता।<br>इस प्रकार केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): केवल I निकलता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000073995","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>In a study of 500 working professionals, those who slept less than 6 hours per night were 3 times more likely to report burnout than those who slept 7-8 hours.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. Sleeping for less than 6 hours is a contributing factor to professional burnout.<br>II. Getting 7-8 hours of sleep eliminates the risk of experiencing burnout. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन दिया गया है, जिसके बाद कुछ निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, चाहे वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों का विरोध करता प्रतीत हो। निष्कर्षों को ध्यानपूर्वक पढ़िए और निर्णय लीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-से दिए गए कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>500 कामकाजी पेशेवरों के एक अध्ययन में, जो प्रति रात 6 घंटे से कम सोते थे, उनमें बर्नआउट की शिकायत 7-8 घंटे सोने वालों की तुलना में 3 गुना अधिक थी।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. 6 घंटे से कम सोना व्यावसायिक बर्नआउट का एक कारक है।<br>II. 7-8 घंटे की नींद बर्नआउट के जोखिम को समाप्त कर देती है। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Inference I follows.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।"},"2":{"en":"Only Inference II follows.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।"},"3":{"en":"Both Inferences I and II follow.","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Neither Inference I nor Inference II follows.","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Less than 6 hours of sleep is linked with 3 times more burnout, so short sleep does contribute to burnout — Inference I follows.<br>The study speaks of higher or lower likelihood, not of removing the risk, so “eliminates the risk” is too strong — Inference II does not follow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only Inference I follows.</b>","hi":"6 घंटे से कम नींद के साथ बर्नआउट 3 गुना अधिक जुड़ा है, अतः कम नींद बर्नआउट में योगदान देती है — निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।<br>अध्ययन संभावना के कम या अधिक होने की बात करता है, जोखिम हटने की नहीं, अतः “जोखिम समाप्त कर देती है” अत्यधिक है — निष्कर्ष II नहीं निकलता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000073996","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Among the four given combinations, two are exactly identical. Identify the matching pair.<br><br>1. Purva Chatterjee, Block-DA, Flat No. 1202, Riversidefront Residency, Salt Lake City, Kolkata – 700091<br>2. Purva Chatterjee, Block D, Flat No. 1202, Riversidefront Residency, Salt Lake City, Kolkata – 700091<br>3. Purva Chatterjee, Block-DA, Flat No. 1202, Riversidefront Residency, Salt Lake City, Kolkata – 700091<br>4. Purva Chatterjee, Block-DA, Flat No.1202, Riverside Front Residency, Salt Lake City, Kolkata – 700091 [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिए गए चार संयोजनों में से दो बिल्कुल समान हैं। मेल खाने वाला युग्म पहचानिए।<br><br>1. Purva Chatterjee, Block-DA, Flat No. 1202, Riversidefront Residency, Salt Lake City, Kolkata – 700091<br>2. Purva Chatterjee, Block D, Flat No. 1202, Riversidefront Residency, Salt Lake City, Kolkata – 700091<br>3. Purva Chatterjee, Block-DA, Flat No. 1202, Riversidefront Residency, Salt Lake City, Kolkata – 700091<br>4. Purva Chatterjee, Block-DA, Flat No.1202, Riverside Front Residency, Salt Lake City, Kolkata – 700091 [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 &amp; 2"},"2":{"en":"2 &amp; 3"},"3":{"en":"1 &amp; 3"},"4":{"en":"3 &amp; 4"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Read the four combinations word by word.<br>1: Block-DA, Flat No. 1202, Riversidefront Residency.<br>2: Block D, Flat No. 1202 — the block is written differently.<br>3: Block-DA, Flat No. 1202, Riversidefront Residency — every word matches line 1.<br>4: Flat No.1202 and Riverside Front Residency — the spacing and the name of the building differ.<br>So 1 and 3 are the identical pair.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 1 &amp; 3.</b>","hi":"चारों संयोजनों को शब्द-दर-शब्द पढ़िए।<br>1: Block-DA, Flat No. 1202, Riversidefront Residency।<br>2: Block D, Flat No. 1202 — ब्लॉक भिन्न लिखा है।<br>3: Block-DA, Flat No. 1202, Riversidefront Residency — हर शब्द पंक्ति 1 से मेल खाता है।<br>4: Flat No.1202 तथा Riverside Front Residency — अंतराल और भवन का नाम भिन्न है।<br>अतः 1 और 3 समान युग्म हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 1 &amp; 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000073997","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"During a project review meeting, you notice that a teammate is visibly distressed, clenching their hands and speaking with a tight, strained voice. When asked if they want to comment, they look down and say, \"I'm fine, don't worry about it.\"<br><br>Which of the following responses by you demonstrates the highest level of emotional intelligence (EQ)? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"परियोजना समीक्षा बैठक के दौरान आप देखते हैं कि एक सहकर्मी स्पष्ट रूप से परेशान है, अपने हाथ कस रहा है और तनावपूर्ण स्वर में बोल रहा है। जब उनसे पूछा जाता है कि क्या वे कुछ कहना चाहते हैं, तो वे नीचे देखकर कहते हैं, \"मैं ठीक हूँ, इसकी चिंता न करें।\"<br><br>आपकी निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी प्रतिक्रिया भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता (EQ) के उच्चतम स्तर को दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Press them immediately during the meeting to share what is wrong so the team can resolve the issue collectively on the spot.","hi":"बैठक के दौरान ही उन पर दबाव डालें कि वे बताएँ क्या गलत है, ताकि टीम मौके पर ही सामूहिक रूप से समस्या हल कर सके।"},"2":{"en":"Accept their verbal response for the duration of the meeting to preserve their privacy, but follow up with them in a private, one-on-one setting later to offer support.","hi":"बैठक के दौरान उनके कहे को स्वीकार करें ताकि उनकी निजता बनी रहे, परंतु बाद में एकांत में व्यक्तिगत रूप से मिलकर सहायता का प्रस्ताव दें।"},"3":{"en":"Take their statement literally, assume they are completely unaffected, and dismiss the physical signs of distress from your mind moving forward.","hi":"उनके कथन को शब्दशः लें, मान लें कि वे पूरी तरह अप्रभावित हैं और आगे से परेशानी के शारीरिक संकेतों को मन से हटा दें।"},"4":{"en":"Immediately approach the department manager after the meeting to report that the teammate appears emotionally unstable and unable to handle the current workload.","hi":"बैठक के बाद तुरंत विभाग प्रबंधक के पास जाकर रिपोर्ट करें कि सहकर्मी भावनात्मक रूप से अस्थिर दिखता है और वर्तमान कार्यभार संभालने में असमर्थ है।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The signs — clenched hands, strained voice, looking down — do not match the words “I'm fine”, so the teammate needs care but not in front of the whole team.<br>Respecting the answer in the meeting protects their dignity, and a private follow-up later gives real support.<br>Pressing them during the meeting embarrasses them, ignoring the signs abandons them, and reporting them as unstable harms their reputation.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Accept their verbal response for the duration of the meeting to preserve their privacy, but follow up with them in a private, one-on-one setting later to offer support.</b>","hi":"संकेत — कसे हुए हाथ, तनावपूर्ण स्वर, नीचे देखना — “मैं ठीक हूँ” कहने से मेल नहीं खाते, अतः सहकर्मी को सहानुभूति चाहिए, परंतु पूरी टीम के सामने नहीं।<br>बैठक में उनके उत्तर का सम्मान करना उनकी गरिमा बचाता है और बाद में एकांत में मिलना वास्तविक सहायता देता है।<br>बैठक में दबाव डालना उन्हें असहज करता है, संकेतों को अनदेखा करना उन्हें अकेला छोड़ता है और अस्थिर बताकर रिपोर्ट करना उनकी साख को नुकसान पहुँचाता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): बैठक के दौरान उनके कहे को स्वीकार करें ताकि उनकी निजता बनी रहे, परंतु बाद में एकांत में व्यक्तिगत रूप से मिलकर सहायता का प्रस्ताव दें।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000073998","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"<b>Read the given conditions carefully and determine the appropriate outcome for the case provided. If any exception applies, identify the authority to whom the case should be referred.</b><br><b>Criteria for Corporate Club Membership:</b><br>(i) Age between 30 and 50 (inclusive).<br>(ii) Salary must be above ₹10 Lakh.<br><b>Exceptions:</b><br><b>Exception (A):</b> If the salary is below ₹10 Lakh but the candidate is a gold-medal athlete, refer the case to the Club Secretary.<br><b>Exception (B):</b> If the candidate meets criteria (i) and (ii) but is currently under a public investigation, refer the case to the Legal Compliance Officer.<br><b>Case:</b> The candidate is 40 years old, has a salary of ₹8 Lakh, and is a gold-medal athlete. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"<b>दी गई शर्तों को ध्यानपूर्वक पढ़िए और दिए गए मामले के लिए उपयुक्त परिणाम निर्धारित कीजिए। यदि कोई अपवाद लागू हो, तो वह प्राधिकारी पहचानिए जिसे मामला भेजा जाना चाहिए।</b><br><b>कॉर्पोरेट क्लब सदस्यता के मानदंड:</b><br>(i) आयु 30 से 50 वर्ष (दोनों सम्मिलित) के बीच हो।<br>(ii) वेतन ₹10 लाख से अधिक हो।<br><b>अपवाद:</b><br><b>अपवाद (A):</b> यदि वेतन ₹10 लाख से कम है, परंतु अभ्यर्थी स्वर्ण पदक विजेता खिलाड़ी है, तो मामला क्लब सचिव को भेजा जाए।<br><b>अपवाद (B):</b> यदि अभ्यर्थी मानदंड (i) और (ii) पूरा करता है, परंतु इस समय सार्वजनिक जाँच के दायरे में है, तो मामला विधि अनुपालन अधिकारी को भेजा जाए।<br><b>मामला:</b> अभ्यर्थी की आयु 40 वर्ष है, वेतन ₹8 लाख है तथा वह स्वर्ण पदक विजेता खिलाड़ी है। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Membership to be granted","hi":"सदस्यता प्रदान की जाए"},"2":{"en":"Case to be referred to the Club Secretary","hi":"मामला क्लब सचिव को भेजा जाए"},"3":{"en":"Membership application to be rejected","hi":"सदस्यता आवेदन अस्वीकार किया जाए"},"4":{"en":"Case to be referred to the Legal Compliance Officer","hi":"मामला विधि अनुपालन अधिकारी को भेजा जाए"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Age 40 ✔ (between 30 and 50).<br>Salary ₹8 Lakh ✘ (not above ₹10 Lakh), so criterion (ii) fails.<br>Exception (A) applies exactly: salary below ₹10 Lakh but the candidate is a gold-medal athlete.<br>So the case goes to the Club Secretary. Exception (B) cannot apply because it needs salary above ₹10 Lakh.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Case to be referred to the Club Secretary.</b>","hi":"आयु 40 ✔ (30 से 50 के बीच)।<br>वेतन ₹8 लाख ✘ (₹10 लाख से अधिक नहीं), अतः मानदंड (ii) पूरा नहीं होता।<br>अपवाद (A) ठीक लागू होता है: वेतन ₹10 लाख से कम, परंतु अभ्यर्थी स्वर्ण पदक विजेता खिलाड़ी है।<br>अतः मामला क्लब सचिव को भेजा जाएगा। अपवाद (B) लागू नहीं हो सकता, क्योंकि उसके लिए वेतन ₹10 लाख से अधिक होना चाहिए।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): मामला क्लब सचिव को भेजा जाए।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000073999","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>A financial authority has mandated more rigorous compliance measures for fintech companies aimed at increasing transparency and defending consumer rights.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Fintech operations require regulatory oversight.<br>II. Transparency is important for protecting consumers. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कथन को ध्यानपूर्वक पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए गए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय लीजिए कि कौन-सा/कौन-से निष्कर्ष तार्किक रूप से कथन से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक वित्तीय प्राधिकरण ने पारदर्शिता बढ़ाने तथा उपभोक्ता अधिकारों की रक्षा के उद्देश्य से फिनटेक कंपनियों के लिए अधिक कड़े अनुपालन उपाय अनिवार्य किए हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. फिनटेक परिचालनों के लिए नियामकीय निगरानी आवश्यक है।<br>II. उपभोक्ताओं की रक्षा के लिए पारदर्शिता महत्वपूर्ण है। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The authority itself imposing compliance measures shows that fintech operations need regulatory oversight — Conclusion I follows.<br>The measures are aimed at increasing transparency to defend consumer rights, so transparency is taken as important for protecting consumers — Conclusion II follows.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Both conclusions I and II follow.</b>","hi":"प्राधिकरण का स्वयं अनुपालन उपाय अनिवार्य करना दर्शाता है कि फिनटेक परिचालनों के लिए नियामकीय निगरानी आवश्यक है — निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।<br>ये उपाय उपभोक्ता अधिकारों की रक्षा के लिए पारदर्शिता बढ़ाने के उद्देश्य से हैं, अतः पारदर्शिता उपभोक्ता-रक्षा के लिए महत्वपूर्ण मानी गई है — निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000074000","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"NOTEBOOK\" is written as \"14otEBO15K\". How will \"RAILWAYS\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"NOTEBOOK\" को \"14otEBO15K\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"RAILWAYS\" को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"18aiLWA24S"},"2":{"en":"18aiLWA25S"},"3":{"en":"18aILWA25S"},"4":{"en":"18AILWA25S"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"NOTEBOOK → 14otEBO15K, letter by letter:<br>N (14) → 14, O → o, T → t, E → E, B → B, O → O, O (15) → 15, K → K<br>So the 1st and 7th letters are written as their alphabet positions and the 2nd and 3rd letters become small.<br>RAILWAYS: R → 18, A → a, I → i, L → L, W → W, A → A, Y (25) → 25, S → S<br>Code = <b>18aiLWA25S</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 18aiLWA25S.</b>","hi":"NOTEBOOK → 14otEBO15K, अक्षर-दर-अक्षर:<br>N (14) → 14, O → o, T → t, E → E, B → B, O → O, O (15) → 15, K → K<br>अर्थात् पहला और सातवाँ अक्षर अपने वर्णमाला क्रमांक के रूप में लिखे जाते हैं और दूसरा तथा तीसरा अक्षर छोटे रूप में आ जाते हैं।<br>RAILWAYS: R → 18, A → a, I → i, L → L, W → W, A → A, Y (25) → 25, S → S<br>कूट = <b>18aiLWA25S</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 18aiLWA25S है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000074001","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, if aBcD is written as bEdG, then how will pQrS be written in that same code language? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में यदि aBcD को bEdG लिखा जाता है, तो उसी कूट भाषा में pQrS को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"qRsT"},"2":{"en":"qTsV"},"3":{"en":"sTuV"},"4":{"en":"pTsV"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"aBcD → bEdG: a + 1 = b, B + 3 = E, c + 1 = d, D + 3 = G, with the case of each letter kept as it is.<br>The pattern is +1, +3, +1, +3.<br>pQrS: p + 1 = q, Q + 3 = T, r + 1 = s, S + 3 = V → <b>qTsV</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): qTsV.</b>","hi":"aBcD → bEdG: a + 1 = b, B + 3 = E, c + 1 = d, D + 3 = G, तथा प्रत्येक अक्षर का बड़ा/छोटा रूप वैसा ही रहता है।<br>पैटर्न है +1, +3, +1, +3।<br>pQrS: p + 1 = q, Q + 3 = T, r + 1 = s, S + 3 = V → <b>qTsV</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): qTsV है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000074002","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Study the pattern in the given series and find the next set of letters in the series.<br>BOM, YSJ, VWG, SAD, ? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दी गई श्रृंखला के पैटर्न का अध्ययन कीजिए और श्रृंखला में अक्षरों का अगला समूह ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>BOM, YSJ, VWG, SAD, ? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PEA"},"2":{"en":"POD"},"3":{"en":"PCZ"},"4":{"en":"QCA"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Compare the terms position by position:<br>B → Y → V → S: each letter moves 3 steps backward (−3)<br>O → S → W → A: each letter moves 4 steps forward (+4)<br>M → J → G → D: each letter moves 3 steps backward (−3)<br>So the next term is S − 3 = P, A + 4 = E, D − 3 = A → <b>PEA</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): PEA.</b>","hi":"पदों की स्थान-दर-स्थान तुलना कीजिए:<br>B → Y → V → S: प्रत्येक अक्षर 3 स्थान पीछे (−3)<br>O → S → W → A: प्रत्येक अक्षर 4 स्थान आगे (+4)<br>M → J → G → D: प्रत्येक अक्षर 3 स्थान पीछे (−3)<br>अतः अगला पद S − 3 = P, A + 4 = E, D − 3 = A → <b>PEA</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): PEA है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000074003","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"The forestry department has decided to implement a total ban on the use of non-biodegradable packaging in all state-managed national parks to protect local wildlife. Which assumption underlies this ban? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"वन विभाग ने स्थानीय वन्यजीवों की सुरक्षा के लिए सभी राज्य-प्रबंधित राष्ट्रीय उद्यानों में गैर-बायोडिग्रेडेबल पैकेजिंग के उपयोग पर पूर्ण प्रतिबंध लागू करने का निर्णय लिया है। इस प्रतिबंध के पीछे कौन-सी पूर्वधारणा है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"There are affordable, biodegradable alternatives readily available for every item currently in use.","hi":"वर्तमान में प्रयोग हो रही प्रत्येक वस्तु के लिए सस्ते और बायोडिग्रेडेबल विकल्प सहज उपलब्ध हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Visitors to the park will comply with the new packaging ban without requiring strict enforcement.","hi":"उद्यान में आने वाले पर्यटक कड़े प्रवर्तन के बिना ही नए पैकेजिंग प्रतिबंध का पालन करेंगे।"},"3":{"en":"The ecosystem in the national parks is currently unable to recover from existing plastic pollution.","hi":"राष्ट्रीय उद्यानों का पारिस्थितिक तंत्र इस समय मौजूद प्लास्टिक प्रदूषण से उबरने में असमर्थ है।"},"4":{"en":"Non-biodegradable waste left by visitors is a direct threat to the health of the local wildlife.","hi":"पर्यटकों द्वारा छोड़ा गया गैर-बायोडिग्रेडेबल कचरा स्थानीय वन्यजीवों के स्वास्थ्य के लिए सीधा खतरा है।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The ban is imposed “to protect local wildlife”, so the department must be assuming that the plastic waste left by visitors actually harms the wildlife.<br>The other options talk about availability of alternatives, visitor compliance or past pollution, none of which is required for the ban to make sense.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Non-biodegradable waste left by visitors is a direct threat to the health of the local wildlife.</b>","hi":"प्रतिबंध “स्थानीय वन्यजीवों की सुरक्षा” के लिए लगाया गया है, अतः विभाग यह मानकर चल रहा है कि पर्यटकों द्वारा छोड़ा गया प्लास्टिक कचरा वास्तव में वन्यजीवों को हानि पहुँचाता है।<br>शेष विकल्प विकल्पों की उपलब्धता, पर्यटकों के अनुपालन या पुराने प्रदूषण की बात करते हैं, जिनमें से कोई भी प्रतिबंध को तर्कसंगत बनाने के लिए आवश्यक नहीं है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): पर्यटकों द्वारा छोड़ा गया गैर-बायोडिग्रेडेबल कचरा स्थानीय वन्यजीवों के स्वास्थ्य के लिए सीधा खतरा है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000074004","section":"REASONING","topic":"Seating & Mixed Arrangement","question":{"en":"Five objects — P, Q, R, S, T — are placed in a row. Q is to the right of P but not adjacent. R is at the left end. S is immediately left of T. T is immediately left of Q. Which arrangement is valid? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"पाँच वस्तुएँ — P, Q, R, S, T — एक पंक्ति में रखी गई हैं। Q, P के दाईं ओर है, परंतु निकटतम नहीं है। R बाएँ छोर पर है। S, T के ठीक बाईं ओर है। T, Q के ठीक बाईं ओर है। कौन-सी व्यवस्था वैध है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"R, P, S, T, Q"},"2":{"en":"P, R, S, T, Q"},"3":{"en":"R, P, T, S, Q"},"4":{"en":"P, S, T, Q, R"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Final arrangement (left to right): R, P, S, T, Q<br><svg width=\"240\" height=\"74\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 74\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><rect x=\"35\" y=\"22\" width=\"34\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"69\" y=\"22\" width=\"34\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"103\" y=\"22\" width=\"34\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"137\" y=\"22\" width=\"34\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"171\" y=\"22\" width=\"34\" height=\"24\"/><path d=\"M120 18V6M116 10l4-4 4 4\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"52\" y=\"39\">R</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\">1</text><text x=\"86\" y=\"39\">P</text><text x=\"86\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\">2</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"39\">S</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\">3</text><text x=\"154\" y=\"39\">T</text><text x=\"154\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\">4</text><text x=\"188\" y=\"39\">Q</text><text x=\"188\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\">5</text><text x=\"128\" y=\"13\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">Facing North</text><text x=\"17\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\">Left</text><text x=\"223\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\">Right</text></g></svg><br>R is at the left end, S, T, Q stand together, and P (2nd) is not adjacent to Q (5th).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): R, P, S, T, Q.</b>","hi":"अंतिम व्यवस्था (बाएँ से दाएँ): R, P, S, T, Q<br><svg width=\"240\" height=\"74\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 74\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><rect x=\"35\" y=\"22\" width=\"34\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"69\" y=\"22\" width=\"34\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"103\" y=\"22\" width=\"34\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"137\" y=\"22\" width=\"34\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"171\" y=\"22\" width=\"34\" height=\"24\"/><path d=\"M120 18V6M116 10l4-4 4 4\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"52\" y=\"39\">R</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\">1</text><text x=\"86\" y=\"39\">P</text><text x=\"86\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\">2</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"39\">S</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\">3</text><text x=\"154\" y=\"39\">T</text><text x=\"154\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\">4</text><text x=\"188\" y=\"39\">Q</text><text x=\"188\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\">5</text><text x=\"128\" y=\"13\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">Facing North</text><text x=\"17\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\">Left</text><text x=\"223\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\">Right</text></g></svg><br>R बाएँ सिरे पर है, S, T, Q साथ-साथ हैं और P (दूसरा) Q (पाँचवाँ) के निकट नहीं है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): R, P, S, T, Q है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000074005","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word. (The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be related to each other based on the number of letters/number of consonants/vowels in the word.)<br><br>Chapter : Book :: Scene : ? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जो तीसरे शब्द से उसी प्रकार संबंधित है जिस प्रकार दूसरा शब्द पहले शब्द से संबंधित है। (शब्दों को सार्थक अंग्रेज़ी शब्द माना जाए और उनका संबंध शब्द में अक्षरों/व्यंजनों/स्वरों की संख्या के आधार पर नहीं होना चाहिए।)<br><br>Chapter : Book :: Scene : ? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Play","hi":"नाटक"},"2":{"en":"Poem","hi":"कविता"},"3":{"en":"Dictionary","hi":"शब्दकोश"},"4":{"en":"Letter","hi":"पत्र"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A chapter is a part of a book.<br>In the same way a scene is a part of a play.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Play.</b>","hi":"अध्याय पुस्तक का एक भाग होता है।<br>उसी प्रकार दृश्य (scene) नाटक का एक भाग होता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): नाटक है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000074006","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Microeconomics","question":{"en":"Which of the following effects does a rise in the price of goods have on consumer surplus? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"वस्तुओं की कीमत में वृद्धि का उपभोक्ता अधिशेष पर क्या प्रभाव पड़ता है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Reduces","hi":"घटाती है"},"2":{"en":"Increases","hi":"बढ़ाती है"},"3":{"en":"Neutral","hi":"तटस्थ"},"4":{"en":"No effect","hi":"कोई प्रभाव नहीं"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Reduces</b><br>Consumer surplus = what a consumer is <b>willing to pay</b> − what he <b>actually pays</b>. When the price rises, the amount actually paid increases, so consumer surplus <b><u>reduces</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The concept of consumer surplus was developed by <b>Alfred Marshall</b>.<br>• Graphically, it is the area <b>below the demand curve and above the price line</b>.<br>• <b>Producer surplus</b> = price received − minimum price the producer will accept.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – घटाती है</b><br>उपभोक्ता अधिशेष = उपभोक्ता जितना <b>देने को तैयार</b> है − जितना वह <b>वास्तव में देता है</b>। कीमत बढ़ने पर वास्तविक भुगतान बढ़ता है, अतः उपभोक्ता अधिशेष <b><u>घटता है</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उपभोक्ता अधिशेष की अवधारणा <b>अल्फ्रेड मार्शल</b> ने विकसित की।<br>• ग्राफ में यह <b>माँग वक्र के नीचे और कीमत रेखा के ऊपर</b> का क्षेत्रफल है।<br>• <b>उत्पादक अधिशेष</b> = प्राप्त कीमत − न्यूनतम कीमत जिस पर उत्पादक बेचने को तैयार है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000074007","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Monetary Policy","question":{"en":"In money supply, M2 refers to which of the following? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मुद्रा आपूर्ति में M2 निम्नलिखित में से किसे दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"M1 + savings deposits with post office savings banks","hi":"M1 + डाकघर बचत बैंकों में बचत जमा"},"2":{"en":"M1 + net time deposits of banks","hi":"M1 + बैंकों की निवल सावधि जमा"},"3":{"en":"M1 - savings deposits with post office savings banks","hi":"M1 - डाकघर बचत बैंकों में बचत जमा"},"4":{"en":"M1 - net time deposits of banks","hi":"M1 - बैंकों की निवल सावधि जमा"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – M1 + savings deposits with post office savings banks</b><br>As per RBI, <b><u>M2 = M1 + savings deposits with post office savings banks</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>M1</b> (narrow money) = currency with public + demand deposits with banks + other deposits with RBI.<br>• <b>M3</b> (broad money) = M1 + net time deposits of banks; <b>M4</b> = M3 + total post office deposits.<br>• M1 is the <b>most liquid</b> and M4 the least liquid measure.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – M1 + डाकघर बचत बैंकों में बचत जमा</b><br>RBI के अनुसार <b><u>M2 = M1 + डाकघर बचत बैंकों में बचत जमा</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>M1</b> (संकुचित मुद्रा) = जनता के पास मुद्रा + बैंकों में माँग जमा + RBI के पास अन्य जमा।<br>• <b>M3</b> (व्यापक मुद्रा) = M1 + बैंकों की निवल सावधि जमा; <b>M4</b> = M3 + डाकघर की कुल जमा।<br>• M1 <b>सर्वाधिक तरल</b> और M4 सबसे कम तरल माप है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000074008","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: World Map","question":{"en":"Which South Asian country is known for its significant textile industry, particularly jute production? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कौन-सा दक्षिण एशियाई देश अपने महत्वपूर्ण वस्त्र उद्योग, विशेषकर जूट उत्पादन के लिए जाना जाता है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Bangladesh","hi":"बांग्लादेश"},"2":{"en":"Pakistan","hi":"पाकिस्तान"},"3":{"en":"Nepal","hi":"नेपाल"},"4":{"en":"Sri Lanka","hi":"श्रीलंका"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Bangladesh</b><br><b><u>Bangladesh</u></b>, in the fertile Ganga–Brahmaputra delta, is a major producer and the largest <b>exporter of raw jute</b>, and its textile/garment industry is the backbone of its exports.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>India</b> is the <b>largest producer</b> of jute; West Bengal leads in India.<br>• Jute is called the <b>\"Golden Fibre\"</b>.<br>• It needs hot humid climate and fertile, flood-renewed <b>alluvial soil</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – बांग्लादेश</b><br>उपजाऊ गंगा–ब्रह्मपुत्र डेल्टा में स्थित <b><u>बांग्लादेश</u></b> जूट का प्रमुख उत्पादक और <b>कच्चे जूट का सबसे बड़ा निर्यातक</b> है, और इसका वस्त्र/परिधान उद्योग इसके निर्यात की रीढ़ है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>भारत</b> जूट का <b>सबसे बड़ा उत्पादक</b> है; भारत में पश्चिम बंगाल अग्रणी है।<br>• जूट को <b>\"सुनहरा रेशा\"</b> कहा जाता है।<br>• इसके लिए गर्म-आर्द्र जलवायु और बाढ़ से नवीकृत उपजाऊ <b>जलोढ़ मिट्टी</b> चाहिए।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000074009","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"How many innings are there in a standard baseball game? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक मानक बेसबॉल खेल में कितनी पारियाँ होती हैं? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"7"},"2":{"en":"8"},"3":{"en":"9"},"4":{"en":"10"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 9</b><br>A standard baseball game has <b><u>9 innings</u></b>; in each inning both teams bat once. Extra innings are played if the score is tied.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Each team has <b>9 players</b> on the field.<br>• Baseball terms: <b>home run, strike, pitcher, diamond</b>.<br>• Baseball is the national pastime of the <b>USA</b>; it returned to the Olympics at <b>Tokyo 2020</b> and will feature at <b>LA 2028</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 9</b><br>एक मानक बेसबॉल खेल में <b><u>9 पारियाँ</u></b> होती हैं; प्रत्येक पारी में दोनों टीमें एक बार बल्लेबाज़ी करती हैं। स्कोर बराबर होने पर अतिरिक्त पारियाँ खेली जाती हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रत्येक टीम के <b>9 खिलाड़ी</b> मैदान में होते हैं।<br>• बेसबॉल के शब्द: <b>होम रन, स्ट्राइक, पिचर, डायमंड</b>।<br>• बेसबॉल <b>अमेरिका</b> का राष्ट्रीय खेल माना जाता है; यह <b>टोक्यो 2020</b> में ओलंपिक में लौटा और <b>LA 2028</b> में भी होगा।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000074010","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Identify the Indian city that hosted the 2017 Asian Athletics Championships. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"2017 एशियाई एथलेटिक्स चैंपियनशिप की मेज़बानी करने वाले भारतीय शहर की पहचान कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Chennai","hi":"चेन्नई"},"2":{"en":"Bhubaneswar","hi":"भुवनेश्वर"},"3":{"en":"Pune","hi":"पुणे"},"4":{"en":"Guwahati","hi":"गुवाहाटी"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Bhubaneswar</b><br>The <b>22<sup>nd</sup> Asian Athletics Championships</b> were held at the <b>Kalinga Stadium</b>, <b><u>Bhubaneswar</u></b>, in <b>July 2017</b>; India topped the medal table for the first time.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India won <b>29 medals (12 gold)</b> at the event.<br>• Odisha also hosted the <b>Men's Hockey World Cup</b> in <b>2018 and 2023</b>.<br>• Odisha is called the <b>\"Sports Capital of India\"</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – भुवनेश्वर</b><br><b>22वीं एशियाई एथलेटिक्स चैंपियनशिप</b> <b>जुलाई 2017</b> में <b><u>भुवनेश्वर</u></b> के <b>कलिंग स्टेडियम</b> में हुई; भारत पहली बार पदक तालिका में शीर्ष पर रहा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत ने इस प्रतियोगिता में <b>29 पदक (12 स्वर्ण)</b> जीते।<br>• ओडिशा ने <b>2018 और 2023</b> में <b>पुरुष हॉकी विश्व कप</b> की भी मेज़बानी की।<br>• ओडिशा को <b>\"भारत की खेल राजधानी\"</b> कहा जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000074011","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"India’s first-ever medal at the Commonwealth Games was won in which year? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"राष्ट्रमंडल खेलों में भारत का पहला पदक किस वर्ष जीता गया? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1934"},"2":{"en":"1958"},"3":{"en":"1966"},"4":{"en":"1970"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – 1934</b><br>India won its first Commonwealth (then British Empire) Games medal in <b><u>1934</u></b> at <b>London</b>, when wrestler <b>Rashid Anwar</b> won bronze.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The first Games were held in <b>1930 at Hamilton, Canada</b>.<br>• India's first CWG gold: <b>Milkha Singh</b> (440 yards, <b>1958 Cardiff</b>).<br>• India hosted the CWG in <b>Delhi (2010)</b> and will host in <b>Ahmedabad (2030)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – 1934</b><br>भारत ने अपना पहला राष्ट्रमंडल (तब ब्रिटिश एम्पायर) खेल पदक <b><u>1934</u></b> में <b>लंदन</b> में जीता, जब पहलवान <b>राशिद अनवर</b> ने कांस्य जीता।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पहले खेल <b>1930 में हैमिल्टन, कनाडा</b> में हुए।<br>• भारत का पहला राष्ट्रमंडल स्वर्ण: <b>मिल्खा सिंह</b> (440 गज, <b>1958 कार्डिफ़</b>)।<br>• भारत ने <b>दिल्ली (2010)</b> में मेज़बानी की और <b>अहमदाबाद (2030)</b> में करेगा।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000074012","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who among the following is the 22<sup>nd</sup> Lieutenant Governor of Delhi? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से दिल्ली के 22वें उपराज्यपाल कौन हैं? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Najeeb Jung","hi":"नजीब जंग"},"2":{"en":"Manoj Sinha","hi":"मनोज सिन्हा"},"3":{"en":"Vinai Kumar Saxena","hi":"विनय कुमार सक्सेना"},"4":{"en":"Anil Baijal","hi":"अनिल बैजल"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Vinai Kumar Saxena</b><br><b><u>Vinai Kumar Saxena</u></b> took charge as the <b>22<sup>nd</sup> Lieutenant Governor of Delhi</b> on <b>26 May 2022</b>, succeeding Anil Baijal.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• He was earlier Chairman of the <b>Khadi and Village Industries Commission (KVIC)</b>.<br>• <b>Anil Baijal</b> was the 21<sup>st</sup> and <b>Najeeb Jung</b> the 20<sup>th</sup> LG.<br>• <b>Manoj Sinha</b> is the LG of <b>Jammu and Kashmir</b>; Delhi's special status is under <b>Article 239AA</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – विनय कुमार सक्सेना</b><br><b><u>विनय कुमार सक्सेना</u></b> ने <b>26 मई 2022</b> को अनिल बैजल के बाद <b>दिल्ली के 22वें उपराज्यपाल</b> का पदभार संभाला।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वे पहले <b>खादी और ग्रामोद्योग आयोग (KVIC)</b> के अध्यक्ष थे।<br>• <b>अनिल बैजल</b> 21वें और <b>नजीब जंग</b> 20वें उपराज्यपाल थे।<br>• <b>मनोज सिन्हा</b> <b>जम्मू और कश्मीर</b> के उपराज्यपाल हैं; दिल्ली का विशेष दर्जा <b>अनुच्छेद 239AA</b> में है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000074013","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Human Geography","question":{"en":"Consider the following specific stages of demographic transition associated with economic development:<br>Select the CORRECT order of the above stages using the codes given below:<br>1. Low birth rate with low death rate.<br>2. High birth rate with high death rate.<br>3. High birth rate with low death rate. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"आर्थिक विकास से जुड़ी जनांकिकीय संक्रमण की निम्नलिखित विशिष्ट अवस्थाओं पर विचार कीजिए:<br>नीचे दिए गए कूटों का प्रयोग करके उपर्युक्त अवस्थाओं का सही क्रम चुनिए:<br>1. निम्न जन्म दर के साथ निम्न मृत्यु दर।<br>2. उच्च जन्म दर के साथ उच्च मृत्यु दर।<br>3. उच्च जन्म दर के साथ निम्न मृत्यु दर। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1-2-3"},"2":{"en":"2-1-3"},"3":{"en":"2-3-1"},"4":{"en":"3-2-1"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 2-3-1</b><br>Demographic transition moves from <b>high birth and high death rates</b> (stage 1) to <b>high birth and falling/low death rates</b> (stage 2, population explosion) and finally to <b>low birth and low death rates</b>. Order: <b><u>2-3-1</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The theory was given by <b>Warren Thompson (1929)</b> and developed by <b>Frank Notestein</b>.<br>• India is currently in the <b>late third stage</b>, with falling birth rates.<br>• Population grows fastest in the <b>second stage</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 2-3-1</b><br>जनांकिकीय संक्रमण <b>उच्च जन्म और उच्च मृत्यु दर</b> (पहली अवस्था) से <b>उच्च जन्म और घटती/निम्न मृत्यु दर</b> (दूसरी अवस्था, जनसंख्या विस्फोट) और अंततः <b>निम्न जन्म और निम्न मृत्यु दर</b> तक जाता है। क्रम: <b><u>2-3-1</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह सिद्धांत <b>वॉरेन थॉम्पसन (1929)</b> ने दिया और <b>फ्रैंक नोटेस्टीन</b> ने विकसित किया।<br>• भारत वर्तमान में घटती जन्म दर के साथ <b>तीसरी अवस्था के अंतिम चरण</b> में है।<br>• जनसंख्या <b>दूसरी अवस्था</b> में सबसे तेज़ी से बढ़ती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000074014","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Monsoon","question":{"en":"According to Koppen’s climatic classification, what does the small letter ‘s’ denote? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कोपेन के जलवायु वर्गीकरण के अनुसार छोटा अक्षर ‘s’ क्या दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"No dry season","hi":"कोई शुष्क ऋतु नहीं"},"2":{"en":"Dry season in winter","hi":"शीत ऋतु में शुष्क मौसम"},"3":{"en":"Dry season in summer","hi":"ग्रीष्म ऋतु में शुष्क मौसम"},"4":{"en":"Rainy season in summer","hi":"ग्रीष्म ऋतु में वर्षा ऋतु"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Dry season in summer</b><br>In Köppen's scheme, <b>'s'</b> means <b><u>dry season in summer</u></b>, <b>'w'</b> means dry season in winter and <b>'f'</b> means no dry season.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>As</b> climate in India – <b>Coromandel coast of Tamil Nadu</b> (dry summer, winter rain).<br>• <b>Amw</b> – west coast south of Goa; <b>Aw</b> – most of the Peninsula.<br>• Köppen used <b>temperature and precipitation</b> data; capital letters A, B, C, D, E denote major climate groups.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – ग्रीष्म ऋतु में शुष्क मौसम</b><br>कोपेन की योजना में <b>'s'</b> का अर्थ <b><u>ग्रीष्म ऋतु में शुष्क मौसम</u></b>, <b>'w'</b> का अर्थ शीत ऋतु में शुष्क मौसम और <b>'f'</b> का अर्थ कोई शुष्क ऋतु नहीं है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत में <b>As</b> जलवायु – <b>तमिलनाडु का कोरोमंडल तट</b> (शुष्क ग्रीष्म, शीतकालीन वर्षा)।<br>• <b>Amw</b> – गोवा के दक्षिण का पश्चिमी तट; <b>Aw</b> – प्रायद्वीप का अधिकांश भाग।<br>• कोपेन ने <b>तापमान और वर्षण</b> के आँकड़ों का प्रयोग किया; बड़े अक्षर A, B, C, D, E प्रमुख जलवायु समूह दर्शाते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000074015","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Vedic Age","question":{"en":"What is the name of the only commonly available school (Shaakha) of the Rigveda today? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"आज ऋग्वेद की एकमात्र सामान्य रूप से उपलब्ध शाखा का नाम क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Maitrayani","hi":"मैत्रायणी"},"2":{"en":"Kauthuma","hi":"कौथुम"},"3":{"en":"Shaakala","hi":"शाकल"},"4":{"en":"Taittiriya","hi":"तैत्तिरीय"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Shaakala</b><br>The <b><u>Shakala Shakha</u></b> is the only complete recension of the <b>Rigveda Samhita</b> available today, with <b>10 mandalas and 1,028 hymns</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Kauthuma</b> – a recension of the <b>Samaveda</b>.<br>• <b>Maitrayani and Taittiriya</b> – recensions of the <b>Krishna Yajurveda</b>.<br>• Mandala III contains the <b>Gayatri Mantra</b>; Mandala X has the <b>Purusha Sukta</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – शाकल</b><br><b><u>शाकल शाखा</u></b> आज उपलब्ध <b>ऋग्वेद संहिता</b> की एकमात्र पूर्ण शाखा है, जिसमें <b>10 मंडल और 1,028 सूक्त</b> हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>कौथुम</b> – <b>सामवेद</b> की शाखा।<br>• <b>मैत्रायणी और तैत्तिरीय</b> – <b>कृष्ण यजुर्वेद</b> की शाखाएँ।<br>• तीसरे मंडल में <b>गायत्री मंत्र</b>; दसवें मंडल में <b>पुरुष सूक्त</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000074016","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"<b>Fill in the blanks:</b><br>The Mando song, known for its emotional depth and cultural fusion, originated in Goa and typically deals with themes such as love, tragedy, and _____. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"<b>रिक्त स्थान भरिए:</b><br>भावनात्मक गहराई और सांस्कृतिक मिश्रण के लिए प्रसिद्ध मांडो गीत की उत्पत्ति गोवा में हुई और यह सामान्यतः प्रेम, त्रासदी और _____ जैसे विषयों से संबंधित है। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"patriotism","hi":"देशभक्ति"},"2":{"en":"colonial resistance","hi":"औपनिवेशिक प्रतिरोध"},"3":{"en":"wedding customs","hi":"विवाह रीतियाँ"},"4":{"en":"mythology","hi":"पौराणिक कथाएँ"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – colonial resistance</b><br>The <b>Mando</b> is a Konkani song form of Goa that blends Indian and Portuguese music. Its themes are <b>love, tragedy</b> and the social/political situation of Portuguese rule, i.e., <b><u>colonial resistance</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Mando developed in the <b>19<sup>th</sup>–20<sup>th</sup> centuries</b>, mainly among Goan Catholics.<br>• It is followed by a faster <b>Dulpod</b> song.<br>• Other Goan folk forms: <b>Fugdi, Dekhni, Dhalo</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – औपनिवेशिक प्रतिरोध</b><br><b>मांडो</b> गोवा का कोंकणी गीत रूप है, जो भारतीय और पुर्तगाली संगीत का मिश्रण है। इसके विषय <b>प्रेम, त्रासदी</b> और पुर्तगाली शासन की सामाजिक/राजनीतिक स्थिति, अर्थात् <b><u>औपनिवेशिक प्रतिरोध</u></b> हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मांडो <b>19वीं–20वीं शताब्दी</b> में मुख्यतः गोवा के कैथोलिकों में विकसित हुआ।<br>• इसके बाद तेज़ लय वाला <b>दुलपोद</b> गीत गाया जाता है।<br>• गोवा के अन्य लोक रूप: <b>फुगडी, देखणी, धालो</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000074017","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"Which committee highlighted the potential of small-scale industries for rural development in 1955? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"1955 में किस समिति ने ग्रामीण विकास के लिए लघु उद्योगों की संभावना को रेखांकित किया? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Narasimham Committee","hi":"नरसिम्हम समिति"},"2":{"en":"Gadgil Committee","hi":"गाडगिल समिति"},"3":{"en":"Karve Committee","hi":"कर्वे समिति"},"4":{"en":"Roy Committee","hi":"रॉय समिति"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Karve Committee</b><br>The <b><u>Karve Committee</u></b> (Village and Small-Scale Industries Committee, 1955) recommended using small-scale industries to promote <b>rural development</b> (NCERT).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Small-scale industries are <b>labour-intensive</b> and generate more employment.<br>• Some goods were <b>reserved</b> for the small-scale sector earlier.<br>• <b>Narasimham Committee</b> (1991, 1998) – banking reforms.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – कर्वे समिति</b><br><b><u>कर्वे समिति</u></b> (ग्राम और लघु उद्योग समिति, 1955) ने <b>ग्रामीण विकास</b> के लिए लघु उद्योगों के उपयोग की सिफारिश की (NCERT)।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• लघु उद्योग <b>श्रम-गहन</b> होते हैं और अधिक रोज़गार देते हैं।<br>• पहले कुछ वस्तुएँ लघु उद्योग क्षेत्र के लिए <b>आरक्षित</b> थीं।<br>• <b>नरसिम्हम समिति</b> (1991, 1998) – बैंकिंग सुधार।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000074018","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Indus Valley Civilization","question":{"en":"Which of the following best describes the architectural layout of the roads and streets in the Lower Town of Mohenjo-Daro? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मोहनजोदड़ो के निचले नगर में सड़कों और गलियों के स्थापत्य विन्यास का सबसे अच्छा वर्णन निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Exact grid pattern","hi":"सटीक ग्रिड पैटर्न"},"2":{"en":"Circular pattern","hi":"वृत्ताकार पैटर्न"},"3":{"en":"Wavy lines pattern","hi":"लहरदार रेखाओं का पैटर्न"},"4":{"en":"Sharp star pattern","hi":"तीखा तारा पैटर्न"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Exact grid pattern</b><br>Roads and streets in the Lower Town of Mohenjo-daro were laid out on an approximate <b><u>grid pattern</u></b>, intersecting at <b>right angles</b> and dividing the town into blocks.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Mohenjo-daro (Sindh) was excavated by <b>R.D. Banerji</b> in <b>1922</b>.<br>• Famous finds: <b>Great Bath, Great Granary, Bronze Dancing Girl, Priest-King</b>.<br>• Houses had covered <b>drains</b> and used <b>baked bricks</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – सटीक ग्रिड पैटर्न</b><br>मोहनजोदड़ो के निचले नगर की सड़कें और गलियाँ लगभग <b><u>ग्रिड पैटर्न</u></b> में बनी थीं, जो <b>समकोण</b> पर काटती थीं और नगर को खंडों में बाँटती थीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मोहनजोदड़ो (सिंध) का उत्खनन <b>आर.डी. बनर्जी</b> ने <b>1922</b> में किया।<br>• प्रसिद्ध खोजें: <b>विशाल स्नानागार, अन्नागार, काँसे की नर्तकी, पुरोहित-राजा</b>।<br>• घरों में ढकी <b>नालियाँ</b> थीं और <b>पकी ईंटों</b> का प्रयोग होता था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000074019","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: India and Its Location","question":{"en":"Which two areas are reflected in the contrasting slope directions of the Indian Desert, indicating the drainage orientation? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारतीय मरुस्थल की विपरीत ढाल दिशाएँ, जो अपवाह दिशा दर्शाती हैं, किन दो क्षेत्रों की ओर संकेत करती हैं? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Punjab Plain and Gujarat Coast","hi":"पंजाब मैदान और गुजरात तट"},"2":{"en":"Sindh region and Rann of Kachchh","hi":"सिंध क्षेत्र और कच्छ का रण"},"3":{"en":"Thar Plateau and Aravalli Range","hi":"थार पठार और अरावली श्रेणी"},"4":{"en":"Indus Basin and Deccan Plateau","hi":"सिंधु बेसिन और दक्कन पठार"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Sindh region and Rann of Kachchh</b><br>The northern part of the Indian Desert slopes towards <b>Sindh</b>, while the southern part slopes towards the <b>Rann of Kachchh</b> – i.e., <b><u>Sindh region and Rann of Kachchh</u></b> (NCERT).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Indian Desert lies <b>north-west of the Aravallis</b>; rainfall is below <b>15 cm</b>.<br>• <b>Luni</b> is the only large river of this region.<br>• Landforms include <b>barchans, longitudinal dunes, playas</b> (salt lakes like Sambhar).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सिंध क्षेत्र और कच्छ का रण</b><br>भारतीय मरुस्थल का उत्तरी भाग <b>सिंध</b> की ओर और दक्षिणी भाग <b>कच्छ के रण</b> की ओर ढलान वाला है – अर्थात् <b><u>सिंध क्षेत्र और कच्छ का रण</u></b> (NCERT)।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारतीय मरुस्थल <b>अरावली के उत्तर-पश्चिम</b> में है; वर्षा <b>15 cm</b> से कम होती है।<br>• <b>लूनी</b> इस क्षेत्र की एकमात्र बड़ी नदी है।<br>• स्थलरूपों में <b>बरखान, अनुदैर्ध्य टिब्बे, प्लाया</b> (सांभर जैसी लवण झीलें) शामिल हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000074020","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: President and Vice President of India","question":{"en":"Under which specific provision of the Indian Constitution is the executive power vested in the President to act as the Supreme Commander of the Defence Forces? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के किस विशिष्ट प्रावधान के तहत राष्ट्रपति को रक्षा बलों के सर्वोच्च कमांडर के रूप में कार्यकारी शक्ति प्रदान की गई है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 61(1)","hi":"अनुच्छेद 61(1)"},"2":{"en":"Article 58(1)","hi":"अनुच्छेद 58(1)"},"3":{"en":"Article 53(2)","hi":"अनुच्छेद 53(2)"},"4":{"en":"Article 56(2)","hi":"अनुच्छेद 56(2)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Article 53(2)</b><br><b><u>Article 53(2)</u></b> states that the <b>supreme command of the Defence Forces</b> of the Union shall be vested in the President, its exercise being regulated by law.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Article 53(1)</b> – executive power of the Union vests in the President.<br>• <b>Article 61</b> – impeachment; <b>Article 58</b> – qualifications; <b>Article 56</b> – term of office.<br>• The President declares war and concludes peace on the advice of the Council of Ministers.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अनुच्छेद 53(2)</b><br><b><u>अनुच्छेद 53(2)</u></b> के अनुसार संघ के <b>रक्षा बलों की सर्वोच्च कमान</b> राष्ट्रपति में निहित होगी, जिसका प्रयोग विधि द्वारा विनियमित होगा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 53(1)</b> – संघ की कार्यपालिका शक्ति राष्ट्रपति में निहित।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 61</b> – महाभियोग; <b>अनुच्छेद 58</b> – योग्यताएँ; <b>अनुच्छेद 56</b> – कार्यकाल।<br>• राष्ट्रपति मंत्रिपरिषद की सलाह पर युद्ध की घोषणा और शांति स्थापित करते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000074021","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Emergency & Constitutional Amendment","question":{"en":"By which Constitutional Amendment Act was Article 246A inserted into the Constitution of India? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किस संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम द्वारा अनुच्छेद 246A भारत के संविधान में जोड़ा गया? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"100<sup>th</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 2015","hi":"100वाँ संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 2015"},"2":{"en":"101<sup>st</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 2016","hi":"101वाँ संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 2016"},"3":{"en":"102<sup>nd</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 2018","hi":"102वाँ संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 2018"},"4":{"en":"103<sup>rd</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 2019","hi":"103वाँ संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 2019"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 101<sup>st</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 2016</b><br><b>Article 246A</b> (special power to make laws on <b>GST</b>) was inserted by the <b><u>101<sup>st</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 2016</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>102<sup>nd</sup> Amendment (2018)</b> – constitutional status to the <b>National Commission for Backward Classes</b> (Art. 338B).<br>• <b>103<sup>rd</sup> Amendment (2019)</b> – <b>10% EWS reservation</b>.<br>• <b>100<sup>th</sup> Amendment (2015)</b> – India–Bangladesh Land Boundary Agreement.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – 101वाँ संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 2016</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 246A</b> (<b>GST</b> पर कानून बनाने की विशेष शक्ति) <b><u>101वें संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 2016</u></b> द्वारा जोड़ा गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>102वाँ संशोधन (2018)</b> – <b>राष्ट्रीय पिछड़ा वर्ग आयोग</b> को संवैधानिक दर्जा (अनु. 338B)।<br>• <b>103वाँ संशोधन (2019)</b> – <b>10% EWS आरक्षण</b>।<br>• <b>100वाँ संशोधन (2015)</b> – भारत–बांग्लादेश भूमि सीमा समझौता।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000074022","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Agriculture","question":{"en":"Which region is most suitable for growing Jowar? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"ज्वार उगाने के लिए कौन-सा क्षेत्र सबसे उपयुक्त है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Humid regions","hi":"आर्द्र क्षेत्र"},"2":{"en":"Semi arid areas","hi":"अर्ध-शुष्क क्षेत्र"},"3":{"en":"Cold regions","hi":"ठंडे क्षेत्र"},"4":{"en":"Coastal regions","hi":"तटीय क्षेत्र"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Semi arid areas</b><br><b>Jowar (sorghum)</b> is a hardy, drought-tolerant millet grown mainly as a rain-fed crop in <b><u>semi-arid areas</u></b> of the Deccan plateau.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Maharashtra</b> is the largest producer of jowar.<br>• Jowar is grown in both <b>Kharif and Rabi</b> seasons.<br>• 2023 was declared the <b>International Year of Millets</b> on India's proposal.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अर्ध-शुष्क क्षेत्र</b><br><b>ज्वार</b> एक सहनशील, सूखा-रोधी मोटा अनाज है जो मुख्यतः दक्कन पठार के <b><u>अर्ध-शुष्क क्षेत्रों</u></b> में वर्षा-आधारित फसल के रूप में उगाया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>महाराष्ट्र</b> ज्वार का सबसे बड़ा उत्पादक है।<br>• ज्वार <b>खरीफ और रबी</b> दोनों मौसमों में उगाई जाती है।<br>• भारत के प्रस्ताव पर 2023 को <b>अंतर्राष्ट्रीय मिलेट वर्ष</b> घोषित किया गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000074023","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: DPSP and Fundamental Duties","question":{"en":"Which of the following is not a Directive Principle of State Policy under Part IV of the Indian Constitution? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन भारतीय संविधान के भाग IV के तहत राज्य के नीति निदेशक तत्वों में नहीं है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Protection of environment","hi":"पर्यावरण का संरक्षण"},"2":{"en":"Right to constitutional remedies","hi":"संवैधानिक उपचारों का अधिकार"},"3":{"en":"Equal pay for equal work","hi":"समान कार्य के लिए समान वेतन"},"4":{"en":"Promotion of village panchayats","hi":"ग्राम पंचायतों को बढ़ावा"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Right to constitutional remedies</b><br>The <b><u>Right to Constitutional Remedies</u></b> (Article 32) is a <b>Fundamental Right</b> in Part III, not a DPSP.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Art. 48A</b> – protection of environment; <b>Art. 39(d)</b> – equal pay for equal work.<br>• <b>Art. 40</b> – organisation of village panchayats.<br>• DPSPs are non-justiciable (<b>Art. 37</b>).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – संवैधानिक उपचारों का अधिकार</b><br><b><u>संवैधानिक उपचारों का अधिकार</u></b> (अनुच्छेद 32) भाग III में <b>मौलिक अधिकार</b> है, नीति निदेशक तत्व नहीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनु. 48A</b> – पर्यावरण संरक्षण; <b>अनु. 39(d)</b> – समान कार्य के लिए समान वेतन।<br>• <b>अनु. 40</b> – ग्राम पंचायतों का संगठन।<br>• नीति निदेशक तत्व गैर-न्यायोचित हैं (<b>अनु. 37</b>)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000074024","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Transport","question":{"en":"Which National Waterway in India includes stretches of the Godavari and Krishna rivers? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत का कौन-सा राष्ट्रीय जलमार्ग गोदावरी और कृष्णा नदियों के खंडों को शामिल करता है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"National Waterway-2","hi":"राष्ट्रीय जलमार्ग-2"},"2":{"en":"National Waterway-3","hi":"राष्ट्रीय जलमार्ग-3"},"3":{"en":"National Waterway-4","hi":"राष्ट्रीय जलमार्ग-4"},"4":{"en":"National Waterway-5","hi":"राष्ट्रीय जलमार्ग-5"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – National Waterway-4</b><br><b><u>National Waterway-4</u></b> includes stretches of the <b>Godavari and Krishna rivers</b> along with the Kakinada–Puducherry canal system.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>NW-1</b> – Ganga–Bhagirathi–Hooghly (Haldia–Prayagraj), longest.<br>• <b>NW-2</b> – Brahmaputra (Dhubri–Sadiya); <b>NW-3</b> – West Coast Canal (Kerala).<br>• <b>NW-5</b> – Brahmani river and East Coast Canal (Odisha–WB); total 111 NWs under the 2016 Act.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – राष्ट्रीय जलमार्ग-4</b><br><b><u>राष्ट्रीय जलमार्ग-4</u></b> में <b>गोदावरी और कृष्णा नदियों</b> के खंड तथा काकीनाडा–पुडुचेरी नहर प्रणाली शामिल है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>NW-1</b> – गंगा–भागीरथी–हुगली (हल्दिया–प्रयागराज), सबसे लंबा।<br>• <b>NW-2</b> – ब्रह्मपुत्र (धुबरी–सादिया); <b>NW-3</b> – पश्चिमी तट नहर (केरल)।<br>• <b>NW-5</b> – ब्राह्मणी नदी और पूर्वी तट नहर (ओडिशा–प.बं.); 2016 अधिनियम के तहत कुल 111 राष्ट्रीय जलमार्ग।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000074025","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"At the 2022 Asian Games held in Hangzhou in 2023, India achieved a historic milestone by crossing which medal count for the first time? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"2023 में हांगझोउ में आयोजित 2022 एशियाई खेलों में भारत ने पहली बार किस पदक संख्या को पार करके ऐतिहासिक उपलब्धि हासिल की? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"50 medals","hi":"50 पदक"},"2":{"en":"75 medals","hi":"75 पदक"},"3":{"en":"100 medals","hi":"100 पदक"},"4":{"en":"150 medals","hi":"150 पदक"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 100 medals</b><br>At the <b>Hangzhou Asian Games</b>, India won <b>107 medals (28 gold, 38 silver, 41 bronze)</b>, crossing the <b><u>100-medal</u></b> mark for the first time.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India finished <b>4<sup>th</sup></b> in the medal table; slogan <b>\"Is baar 100 paar\"</b>.<br>• <b>Neeraj Chopra</b> won javelin gold; <b>cricket</b> was included and India won both men's and women's gold.<br>• The first Asian Games were held in <b>New Delhi (1951)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 100 पदक</b><br><b>हांगझोउ एशियाई खेलों</b> में भारत ने <b>107 पदक (28 स्वर्ण, 38 रजत, 41 कांस्य)</b> जीते और पहली बार <b><u>100 पदक</u></b> का आँकड़ा पार किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत पदक तालिका में <b>चौथे</b> स्थान पर रहा; नारा <b>\"इस बार 100 पार\"</b>।<br>• <b>नीरज चोपड़ा</b> ने भाला फेंक स्वर्ण जीता; <b>क्रिकेट</b> शामिल हुआ और भारत ने पुरुष व महिला दोनों स्वर्ण जीते।<br>• पहले एशियाई खेल <b>नई दिल्ली (1951)</b> में हुए।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000074026","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: National Parks","question":{"en":"As of April 2026, what is the total number of notified Biosphere Reserves in India, and how many among them are part of UNESCO's World Network of Biosphere Reserves (WNBR)? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"अप्रैल 2026 तक भारत में अधिसूचित जैवमंडल आरक्षित क्षेत्रों की कुल संख्या क्या है और उनमें से कितने यूनेस्को के जैवमंडल आरक्षित क्षेत्रों के विश्व नेटवर्क (WNBR) का हिस्सा हैं? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"18 Biosphere Reserves and 10 WNBR","hi":"18 जैवमंडल आरक्षित क्षेत्र और 10 WNBR"},"2":{"en":"18 Biosphere Reserves and 13 WNBR","hi":"18 जैवमंडल आरक्षित क्षेत्र और 13 WNBR"},"3":{"en":"20 Biosphere Reserves and 13 WNBR","hi":"20 जैवमंडल आरक्षित क्षेत्र और 13 WNBR"},"4":{"en":"20 Biosphere Reserves and 11 WNBR","hi":"20 जैवमंडल आरक्षित क्षेत्र और 11 WNBR"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 18 Biosphere Reserves and 13 WNBR</b><br>India has <b><u>18 notified Biosphere Reserves</u></b>, of which <b><u>13</u></b> are in UNESCO's <b>World Network of Biosphere Reserves</b>; the <b>Cold Desert Biosphere Reserve</b> (Himachal Pradesh) was added to the WNBR in <b>2025</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India's first Biosphere Reserve: <b>Nilgiri (1986)</b>, also the first to join the WNBR (2000).<br>• Largest BR: <b>Gulf of Kachchh / Rann of Kutch</b> area.<br>• WNBR works under UNESCO's <b>Man and the Biosphere (MAB) Programme (1971)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – 18 जैवमंडल आरक्षित क्षेत्र और 13 WNBR</b><br>भारत में <b><u>18 अधिसूचित जैवमंडल आरक्षित क्षेत्र</u></b> हैं, जिनमें से <b><u>13</u></b> यूनेस्को के <b>जैवमंडल आरक्षित क्षेत्रों के विश्व नेटवर्क</b> में हैं; <b>शीत मरुस्थल जैवमंडल आरक्षित क्षेत्र</b> (हिमाचल प्रदेश) <b>2025</b> में WNBR में जोड़ा गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत का पहला जैवमंडल आरक्षित क्षेत्र: <b>नीलगिरि (1986)</b>, जो WNBR में शामिल होने वाला भी पहला (2000) था।<br>• सबसे बड़ा जैवमंडल: <b>कच्छ की खाड़ी / कच्छ का रण</b> क्षेत्र।<br>• WNBR यूनेस्को के <b>मानव और जैवमंडल (MAB) कार्यक्रम (1971)</b> के तहत कार्य करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000074027","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"The foreign investment limit in banks was raised to around what percentage under the 1991 reform policies? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"1991 की सुधार नीतियों के तहत बैंकों में विदेशी निवेश की सीमा को लगभग कितने प्रतिशत तक बढ़ाया गया? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"49%"},"2":{"en":"51%"},"3":{"en":"74%"},"4":{"en":"100%"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 74%</b><br>As per NCERT (Indian Economic Development), under financial sector reforms the <b>foreign investment limit in banks</b> was raised to around <b><u>74%</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Financial sector reforms reduced the role of RBI from <b>regulator to facilitator</b>.<br>• <b>Foreign Institutional Investors (FIIs)</b> were allowed to invest in Indian financial markets.<br>• Public sector banks' FDI cap is <b>20%</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 74%</b><br>NCERT (भारतीय आर्थिक विकास) के अनुसार वित्तीय क्षेत्र सुधारों के तहत <b>बैंकों में विदेशी निवेश की सीमा</b> को लगभग <b><u>74%</u></b> तक बढ़ाया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वित्तीय क्षेत्र सुधारों ने RBI की भूमिका को <b>नियामक से सुविधाप्रदाता</b> की ओर बदला।<br>• <b>विदेशी संस्थागत निवेशकों (FII)</b> को भारतीय वित्तीय बाज़ारों में निवेश की अनुमति मिली।<br>• सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र के बैंकों में FDI सीमा <b>20%</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000074028","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Post-Gupta Dynasties","question":{"en":"The Harshacharita was composed by which writer? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"हर्षचरित की रचना किस लेखक ने की? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Kalidasa","hi":"कालिदास"},"2":{"en":"Banabhatta","hi":"बाणभट्ट"},"3":{"en":"Dandin","hi":"दंडी"},"4":{"en":"Bharata","hi":"भरत"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Banabhatta</b><br><b>Harshacharita</b>, the biography of King <b>Harshavardhana</b> in Sanskrit, was composed by his court poet <b><u>Banabhatta</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Banabhatta also wrote <b>Kadambari</b>.<br>• Harsha himself wrote three plays: <b>Ratnavali, Priyadarshika, Nagananda</b>.<br>• Chinese pilgrim <b>Hiuen Tsang</b> visited India during Harsha's reign.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – बाणभट्ट</b><br>राजा <b>हर्षवर्धन</b> की संस्कृत जीवनी <b>हर्षचरित</b> की रचना उनके दरबारी कवि <b><u>बाणभट्ट</u></b> ने की।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बाणभट्ट ने <b>कादंबरी</b> भी लिखी।<br>• हर्ष ने स्वयं तीन नाटक लिखे: <b>रत्नावली, प्रियदर्शिका, नागानंद</b>।<br>• हर्ष के शासनकाल में चीनी यात्री <b>ह्वेनसांग</b> भारत आया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000074029","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Which of the following was an outcome of the devaluation of the rupee under India's foreign exchange reforms of 1991? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"1991 के भारत के विदेशी विनिमय सुधारों के तहत रुपये के अवमूल्यन का परिणाम निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा था? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Decline in foreign exchange inflows.","hi":"विदेशी मुद्रा प्रवाह में गिरावट।"},"2":{"en":"Increase in the inflow of foreign exchange.","hi":"विदेशी मुद्रा के प्रवाह में वृद्धि।"},"3":{"en":"Complete abolition of exchange controls.","hi":"विनिमय नियंत्रणों का पूर्ण उन्मूलन।"},"4":{"en":"Replacement of the rupee by a foreign currency.","hi":"रुपये के स्थान पर विदेशी मुद्रा का प्रयोग।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Increase in the inflow of foreign exchange.</b><br>The rupee was devalued in 1991 to solve the BoP crisis. Cheaper Indian exports led to an <b><u>increase in the inflow of foreign exchange</u></b> (NCERT).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The rupee was devalued in <b>two steps in July 1991</b> (about 18–19%).<br>• The exchange rate was later made <b>market-determined</b> (1993).<br>• <b>FEMA, 1999</b> replaced <b>FERA, 1973</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – विदेशी मुद्रा के प्रवाह में वृद्धि।</b><br>भुगतान संतुलन संकट दूर करने के लिए 1991 में रुपये का अवमूल्यन किया गया। भारतीय निर्यात सस्ते होने से <b><u>विदेशी मुद्रा के प्रवाह में वृद्धि</u></b> हुई (NCERT)।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• रुपये का अवमूल्यन <b>जुलाई 1991 में दो चरणों</b> में (लगभग 18–19%) हुआ।<br>• बाद में विनिमय दर को <b>बाज़ार-निर्धारित</b> (1993) बनाया गया।<br>• <b>FEMA, 1999</b> ने <b>FERA, 1973</b> का स्थान लिया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000074030","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Why can a constant-volume gas thermometer provide nearly the same temperature reading regardless of the gas used? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"स्थिर-आयतन गैस तापमापी उपयोग की गई गैस से निरपेक्ष लगभग समान तापमान पाठ्यांक क्यों दे सकता है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The density of every gas is kept identical at all temperatures.","hi":"प्रत्येक गैस का घनत्व सभी तापमानों पर समान रखा जाता है।"},"2":{"en":"Gas pressure becomes independent of changes in volume.","hi":"गैस का दाब आयतन परिवर्तन से स्वतंत्र हो जाता है।"},"3":{"en":"Real gases approach ideal-gas behaviour at sufficiently low pressure.","hi":"पर्याप्त कम दाब पर वास्तविक गैसें आदर्श गैस जैसा व्यवहार करने लगती हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Mercury expansion compensates for the non-ideal behaviour of gases.","hi":"पारे का प्रसार गैसों के अनादर्श व्यवहार की क्षतिपूर्ति करता है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Real gases approach ideal-gas behaviour at sufficiently low pressure.</b><br>At low pressure and low density, all <b>real gases behave like an ideal gas</b>, for which \\(P \\propto T\\) at constant volume. Hence <b><u>real gases approach ideal-gas behaviour at sufficiently low pressure</u></b>, and the reading is almost independent of the gas used.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Gas thermometers are used as <b>standard thermometers</b> for calibration.<br>• Extrapolating P to zero gives <b>absolute zero (−273.15 °C = 0 K)</b>.<br>• <b>Gay-Lussac's law</b>: at constant volume, pressure ∝ absolute temperature.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – पर्याप्त कम दाब पर वास्तविक गैसें आदर्श गैस जैसा व्यवहार करने लगती हैं।</b><br>कम दाब और कम घनत्व पर सभी <b>वास्तविक गैसें आदर्श गैस की तरह व्यवहार</b> करती हैं, जिसके लिए स्थिर आयतन पर \\(P \\propto T\\) होता है। अतः <b><u>पर्याप्त कम दाब पर वास्तविक गैसें आदर्श गैस व्यवहार के निकट पहुँचती हैं</u></b>, और पाठ्यांक प्रयुक्त गैस से लगभग स्वतंत्र होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• गैस तापमापी को अंशांकन हेतु <b>मानक तापमापी</b> के रूप में प्रयोग किया जाता है।<br>• P को शून्य तक बहिर्वेशित करने पर <b>परम शून्य (−273.15 °C = 0 K)</b> मिलता है।<br>• <b>गे-लुसाक का नियम</b>: स्थिर आयतन पर दाब ∝ परम ताप।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000074031","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The base area of a right prism is 72 cm² and height is 15 cm. Find volume. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक लंब प्रिज़्म का आधार क्षेत्रफल 72 cm² और ऊँचाई 15 cm है। आयतन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1000 cm³"},"2":{"en":"1080 cm³"},"3":{"en":"1100 cm³"},"4":{"en":"1150 cm³"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Volume \\(= \\) base area \\(\\times\\) height<br>\\(= 72 \\times 15\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1080\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1080 cm³.</b>","hi":"आयतन \\(= \\) आधार क्षेत्रफल \\(\\times\\) ऊँचाई<br>\\(= 72 \\times 15\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1080\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1080 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000074032","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"The perimeter of an equilateral triangle is 36 cm. Find the area of the triangle. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक समबाहु त्रिभुज का परिमाप 36 cm है। त्रिभुज का क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(46\\sqrt{3}\\) cm²"},"2":{"en":"\\(37\\sqrt{3}\\) cm²"},"3":{"en":"\\(36\\sqrt{3}\\) cm²"},"4":{"en":"\\(26\\sqrt{3}\\) cm²"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"222\" height=\"199\" viewBox=\"0 0 222 199\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M111 26L26 173L196 173Z\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"111\" y=\"16\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"184\">B</text><text x=\"209\" y=\"184\">C</text><text x=\"47\" y=\"91\">12 cm</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"91\">12 cm</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"189\">12 cm</text></g></svg><br>Side \\(= \\frac{36}{3} = 12\\) cm<br>Area \\(= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\times 144 = 36\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{36\\sqrt{3}\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(36\\sqrt{3}\\) cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"222\" height=\"199\" viewBox=\"0 0 222 199\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M111 26L26 173L196 173Z\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"111\" y=\"16\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"184\">B</text><text x=\"209\" y=\"184\">C</text><text x=\"47\" y=\"91\">12 cm</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"91\">12 cm</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"189\">12 cm</text></g></svg><br>भुजा \\(= \\frac{36}{3} = 12\\) cm<br>क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\times 144 = 36\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{36\\sqrt{3}\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(36\\sqrt{3}\\) cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000074033","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A solid cylinder is melted and reshaped into 4 identical smaller cylinders. What will be the volume of each of the smaller cylinders? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक ठोस बेलन को पिघलाकर 4 समान छोटे बेलनों में ढाला जाता है। प्रत्येक छोटे बेलन का आयतन क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1/2 original","hi":"मूल का 1/2"},"2":{"en":"1/4 original","hi":"मूल का 1/4"},"3":{"en":"same as original","hi":"मूल के समान"},"4":{"en":"1/3 original","hi":"मूल का 1/3"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Melting conserves volume<br>Volume of each \\(= \\frac{1}{4}\\) of the original \\(= \\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}\\ \\text{original}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1/4 original.</b>","hi":"पिघलाने पर आयतन संरक्षित रहता है<br>प्रत्येक का आयतन \\(= \\) मूल का \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) \\(= \\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}\\ \\text{original}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): मूल का 1/4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000074034","section":"MATH","topic":"Partnership","question":{"en":"A and B invest in a business in a ratio of 3:2. Five percent of the total profit is donated to charity, and A's share amounts to ₹855. What is the total profit? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"A और B किसी व्यवसाय में 3:2 के अनुपात में निवेश करते हैं। कुल लाभ का पाँच प्रतिशत दान में दिया जाता है और A का हिस्सा ₹855 है। कुल लाभ क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹1,425"},"2":{"en":"₹1,500"},"3":{"en":"₹1,537"},"4":{"en":"₹1,700"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Distributable profit \\(= 95\\%\\) of total, shared 3 : 2<br>A's share \\(= \\frac{3}{5} \\times 0.95P = 0.57P = 855\\)<br>₹\\(P = \\frac{855}{0.57} = \\boxed{1{,}500}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹1,500.</b>","hi":"बाँटने योग्य लाभ \\(= \\) कुल का 95%, 3 : 2 में<br>A का हिस्सा \\(= \\frac{3}{5} \\times 0.95P = 0.57P = 855\\)<br>₹\\(P = \\frac{855}{0.57} = \\boxed{1{,}500}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹1,500 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000074035","section":"MATH","topic":"Time Speed and Distance","question":{"en":"A person covers half of his journey at 40 km/h and the remaining half at 60 km/h. Determine his average speed for the entire journey. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति अपनी यात्रा का आधा भाग 40 km/h और शेष आधा 60 km/h की गति से तय करता है। पूरी यात्रा की औसत गति ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"54 km/h"},"2":{"en":"65 km/h"},"3":{"en":"48 km/h"},"4":{"en":"87 km/h"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Equal distances: average speed \\(= \\frac{2xy}{x + y}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{2 \\times 40 \\times 60}{100}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{48\\ \\text{km/h}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 48 km/h.</b>","hi":"समान दूरियाँ: औसत गति \\(= \\frac{2xy}{x + y}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{2 \\times 40 \\times 60}{100}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{48\\ \\text{km/h}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 48 km/h है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000074036","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"Find the compound interest on ₹5,000 at 12% per annum for 1 year 4 months, compounded annually. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"₹5,000 पर 12% प्रति वर्ष की दर से 1 वर्ष 4 महीने का चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज ज्ञात कीजिए, जो वार्षिक रूप से संयोजित होता है। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹824"},"2":{"en":"₹804"},"3":{"en":"₹900"},"4":{"en":"₹800"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"1 year: \\(5000 \\times 1.12 = 5600\\)<br>For the remaining 4 months (fractional period): \\(5600\\left(1 + \\frac{4}{12} \\times 0.12\\right) = 5600 \\times 1.04 = 5824\\)<br>CI ₹\\(= 5824 - 5000 = \\boxed{824}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ₹824.</b>","hi":"1 वर्ष: \\(5000 \\times 1.12 = 5600\\)<br>शेष 4 महीनों के लिए: \\(5600\\left(1 + \\frac{4}{12} \\times 0.12\\right) = 5600 \\times 1.04 = 5824\\)<br>CI ₹\\(= 5824 - 5000 = \\boxed{824}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ₹824 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000074037","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"The area of a rectangle with a breadth of 9 cm is equal to the area of a square whose side measures 12 cm. Determine the length of the rectangle. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"9 cm चौड़ाई वाले एक आयत का क्षेत्रफल उस वर्ग के क्षेत्रफल के बराबर है जिसकी भुजा 12 cm है। आयत की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"21 cm"},"2":{"en":"11 cm"},"3":{"en":"18 cm"},"4":{"en":"16 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Square area \\(= 144\\) cm²<br>\\(9L = 144 \\Rightarrow L = \\frac{144}{9}\\)<br>\\(L = \\boxed{16\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 16 cm.</b>","hi":"वर्ग का क्षेत्रफल \\(= 144\\) cm²<br>\\(9L = 144 \\Rightarrow L = \\frac{144}{9}\\)<br>\\(L = \\boxed{16\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 16 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000074038","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A cone has a volume of 300π cm³ and a height of 9 cm. Find the radius of its base. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक शंकु का आयतन 300π cm³ और ऊँचाई 9 cm है। उसके आधार की त्रिज्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6 cm"},"2":{"en":"15 cm"},"3":{"en":"18 cm"},"4":{"en":"10 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"202\" height=\"144\" viewBox=\"0 0 202 144\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 94A75 24 0 0 0 176 94M26 94L101 26L176 94M107 94L107 88L101 88\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 94A75 24 0 0 1 176 94M101 26L101 94M101 94L176 94\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"94\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"106\" y=\"67\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">9 cm</text><text x=\"138\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"11\">r</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 \\times 9 = 300\\pi\\)<br>\\(3r^2 = 300 \\Rightarrow r^2 = 100\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{10\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 10 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"202\" height=\"144\" viewBox=\"0 0 202 144\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 94A75 24 0 0 0 176 94M26 94L101 26L176 94M107 94L107 88L101 88\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 94A75 24 0 0 1 176 94M101 26L101 94M101 94L176 94\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"94\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"106\" y=\"67\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">9 cm</text><text x=\"138\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"11\">r</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 \\times 9 = 300\\pi\\)<br>\\(3r^2 = 300 \\Rightarrow r^2 = 100\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{10\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 10 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000074039","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"The ratio of the areas of two concentric circles is 25: 16. If the width of the ring formed is 9 m, find the radius of the smaller circle. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दो संकेंद्री वृत्तों के क्षेत्रफलों का अनुपात 25:16 है। यदि बनने वाले वलय की चौड़ाई 9 m है, तो छोटे वृत्त की त्रिज्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20 m"},"2":{"en":"45 m"},"3":{"en":"28 m"},"4":{"en":"36 m"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"230\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 230 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M179 111L196 111\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M111 111L196 111\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"111\" r=\"85\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"111\" r=\"68\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"111\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"145\" y=\"108\">r</text><text x=\"202\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"start\">9 m</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"108\">O</text></g></svg><br>Area ratio \\(25 : 16\\) → radii ratio \\(5 : 4\\)<br>\\(5x - 4x = 9 \\Rightarrow x = 9\\)<br>Smaller radius \\(= 4 \\times 9 = \\boxed{36\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 36 m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"230\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 230 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M179 111L196 111\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M111 111L196 111\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"111\" r=\"85\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"111\" r=\"68\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"111\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"145\" y=\"108\">r</text><text x=\"202\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"start\">9 m</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"108\">O</text></g></svg><br>क्षेत्रफल अनुपात \\(25 : 16\\) → त्रिज्या अनुपात \\(5 : 4\\)<br>\\(5x - 4x = 9 \\Rightarrow x = 9\\)<br>छोटी त्रिज्या \\(= 4 \\times 9 = \\boxed{36\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 36 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000074040","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"A ladder leaning against a wall makes an angle of 30° with the ground. If the length of the ladder is 10 m, find the distance of the foot of the ladder from the wall. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दीवार के सहारे झुकी एक सीढ़ी जमीन से 30° का कोण बनाती है। यदि सीढ़ी की लंबाई 10 m है, तो सीढ़ी के तल की दीवार से दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6.66 m"},"2":{"en":"9.66 m"},"3":{"en":"8.66 m"},"4":{"en":"7.66 m"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"261\" height=\"173\" viewBox=\"-9 0 261 173\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 26L26 147L226 147M208 147L26 42M34 147L34 139L26 139M190 147A18 18 0 0 1 192 138\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"179\" y=\"143\" font-size=\"11\">30°</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"82\">10 m</text><text x=\"117\" y=\"163\">d</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"46\">A</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"158\">B</text><text x=\"216\" y=\"158\">C</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"30\" text-anchor=\"end\">Wall</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\cos 30° = \\frac{d}{10}\\)<br>\\(d = 10 \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} = 5\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(d = \\boxed{8.66\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 8.66 m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"261\" height=\"173\" viewBox=\"-9 0 261 173\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 26L26 147L226 147M208 147L26 42M34 147L34 139L26 139M190 147A18 18 0 0 1 192 138\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"179\" y=\"143\" font-size=\"11\">30°</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"82\">10 m</text><text x=\"117\" y=\"163\">d</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"46\">A</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"158\">B</text><text x=\"216\" y=\"158\">C</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"30\" text-anchor=\"end\">Wall</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\cos 30° = \\frac{d}{10}\\)<br>\\(d = 10 \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} = 5\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(d = \\boxed{8.66\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 8.66 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000074041","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In a circle with centre O, AB is a chord, and C lies on the minor arc AB. Tangents at points A and B meet at point P. If ∠ACB = 120°, then what is the measure of ∠APB? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"केंद्र O वाले वृत्त में AB एक जीवा है और C लघु चाप AB पर स्थित है। बिंदुओं A और B पर स्पर्श रेखाएँ बिंदु P पर मिलती हैं। यदि ∠ACB = 120° है, तो ∠APB का माप क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"30°"},"2":{"en":"45°"},"3":{"en":"60°"},"4":{"en":"120°"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"179\" height=\"242\" viewBox=\"0 0 179 242\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M34 121L89 26L144 121M40 124L43 119L37 116M139 124L136 119L141 116M34 121L89 89L144 121M81 94A10 10 0 0 0 98 94M83 36A12 12 0 0 0 95 36\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M89 153L34 121M89 153L144 121\"/><circle cx=\"89\" cy=\"153\" r=\"63\"/><circle cx=\"89\" cy=\"153\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"89\" y=\"169\">O</text><text x=\"21\" y=\"118\">A</text><text x=\"158\" y=\"118\">B</text><text x=\"89\" y=\"23\">P</text><text x=\"89\" y=\"86\">C</text><text x=\"89\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"11\">120°</text><text x=\"89\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"11\">?</text></g></svg><br>C on the minor arc → the reflex (major-arc) angle at the centre: \\(\\angle AOB = 2(180° - 120°) = 120°\\)<br>In quadrilateral OAPB: \\(\\angle APB = 180° - 120°\\)<br>\\(\\angle APB = \\boxed{60°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 60°.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"179\" height=\"242\" viewBox=\"0 0 179 242\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M34 121L89 26L144 121M40 124L43 119L37 116M139 124L136 119L141 116M34 121L89 89L144 121M81 94A10 10 0 0 0 98 94M83 36A12 12 0 0 0 95 36\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M89 153L34 121M89 153L144 121\"/><circle cx=\"89\" cy=\"153\" r=\"63\"/><circle cx=\"89\" cy=\"153\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"89\" y=\"169\">O</text><text x=\"21\" y=\"118\">A</text><text x=\"158\" y=\"118\">B</text><text x=\"89\" y=\"23\">P</text><text x=\"89\" y=\"86\">C</text><text x=\"89\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"11\">120°</text><text x=\"89\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"11\">?</text></g></svg><br>C लघु चाप पर है → केंद्र पर प्रतिवर्त (दीर्घ चाप) कोण: \\(\\angle AOB = 2(180° - 120°) = 120°\\)<br>चतुर्भुज OAPB में: \\(\\angle APB = 180° - 120°\\)<br>\\(\\angle APB = \\boxed{60°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 60° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000074042","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If cot A = 7, then find the value of \\(\\frac{5\\cos A + 4\\sin A}{\\cos^3 A + 7\\sin^3 A + 6\\sin A}\\). [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि cot A = 7 है, तो \\(\\frac{5\\cos A + 4\\sin A}{\\cos^3 A + 7\\sin^3 A + 6\\sin A}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"3"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"With \\(\\cot A = 7\\), take \\(\\cos A = 7k\\), \\(\\sin A = k\\) where \\(k = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{50}}\\)<br>\\(\\cos^3A + 7\\sin^3A = k^3(343 + 7) = 350k^3 = 7k = \\cos A\\)<br>So the expression becomes \\(\\frac{5\\cos A + 4\\sin A}{\\cos A + 6\\sin A}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{35k + 4k}{7k + 6k} = \\frac{39}{13} = \\boxed{3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 3.</b>","hi":"\\(\\cot A = 7\\) के लिए \\(\\cos A = 7k\\), \\(\\sin A = k\\) लीजिए, जहाँ \\(k = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{50}}\\)<br>\\(\\cos^3A + 7\\sin^3A = k^3(343 + 7) = 350k^3 = 7k = \\cos A\\)<br>अतः व्यंजक बन जाता है \\(\\frac{5\\cos A + 4\\sin A}{\\cos A + 6\\sin A}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{35k + 4k}{7k + 6k} = \\frac{39}{13} = \\boxed{3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000074043","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Solve: \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2} + 1} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4} + \\sqrt{3}}\\). [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"हल कीजिए: \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2} + 1} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4} + \\sqrt{3}}\\)। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Each term rationalises: \\((\\sqrt{2} - 1) + (\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}) + (2 - \\sqrt{3})\\)<br>All intermediate terms cancel<br>\\(= 2 - 1 = \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद का परिमेयकरण: \\((\\sqrt{2} - 1) + (\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}) + (2 - \\sqrt{3})\\)<br>मध्य पद कट जाते हैं<br>\\(= 2 - 1 = \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000074044","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"If √3 = 1.732, then find the value of \\(\\frac{6\\sqrt{3} + 9}{\\sqrt{3}}\\). [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि √3 = 1.732 है, तो \\(\\frac{6\\sqrt{3} + 9}{\\sqrt{3}}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2.457"},"2":{"en":"11.196"},"3":{"en":"14.786"},"4":{"en":"4.652"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{6\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} + \\frac{9}{\\sqrt{3}} = 6 + 3\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(= 6 + 3(1.732) = 6 + 5.196\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{11.196}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 11.196.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{6\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} + \\frac{9}{\\sqrt{3}} = 6 + 3\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(= 6 + 3(1.732) = 6 + 5.196\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{11.196}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 11.196 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000074045","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A spherical iron ball of radius 3 cm is dropped into a cylindrical tub of radius 4 cm containing water. By how much will the water level rise? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"3 cm त्रिज्या की एक लोहे की गोलाकार गेंद 4 cm त्रिज्या वाले पानी से भरे बेलनाकार टब में डाली जाती है। पानी का स्तर कितना बढ़ेगा? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1.25 cm"},"2":{"en":"2.25 cm"},"3":{"en":"3.78 cm"},"4":{"en":"5.78 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"187\" height=\"232\" viewBox=\"0 0 187 232\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 186A62 20 0 0 0 150 186M26 186L26 47M150 186L150 47\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 186A62 20 0 0 1 150 186M88 47L150 47M88 137L135 137\"/><ellipse cx=\"88\" cy=\"47\" rx=\"62\" ry=\"20\"/><ellipse cx=\"88\" cy=\"81\" rx=\"62\" ry=\"20\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><ellipse cx=\"88\" cy=\"46\" rx=\"62\" ry=\"20\"/><circle cx=\"88\" cy=\"137\" r=\"47\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"171\" y=\"67\">rise</text><text x=\"119\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"11\">4 cm</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"133\" font-size=\"11\">3 cm</text></g></svg><br>Sphere volume \\(= \\frac{4}{3}\\pi(27) = 36\\pi\\)<br>Rise \\(= \\frac{36\\pi}{\\pi(16)} = \\frac{36}{16}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{2.25\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2.25 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"187\" height=\"232\" viewBox=\"0 0 187 232\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 186A62 20 0 0 0 150 186M26 186L26 47M150 186L150 47\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 186A62 20 0 0 1 150 186M88 47L150 47M88 137L135 137\"/><ellipse cx=\"88\" cy=\"47\" rx=\"62\" ry=\"20\"/><ellipse cx=\"88\" cy=\"81\" rx=\"62\" ry=\"20\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><ellipse cx=\"88\" cy=\"46\" rx=\"62\" ry=\"20\"/><circle cx=\"88\" cy=\"137\" r=\"47\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"171\" y=\"67\">rise</text><text x=\"119\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"11\">4 cm</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"133\" font-size=\"11\">3 cm</text></g></svg><br>गोले का आयतन \\(= \\frac{4}{3}\\pi(27) = 36\\pi\\)<br>वृद्धि \\(= \\frac{36\\pi}{\\pi(16)} = \\frac{36}{16}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{2.25\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 2.25 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000074046","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In triangle ABC, points D and E lie on sides AB and AC, respectively, such that AD × AC = AB × AE. If ∠ABC = 75° and ∠ADE exceeds ∠ACB by 25°, determine the measure of ∠A. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"त्रिभुज ABC में, बिंदु D और E क्रमशः भुजाओं AB और AC पर इस प्रकार हैं कि AD × AC = AB × AE है। यदि ∠ABC = 75° और ∠ADE, ∠ACB से 25° अधिक है, तो ∠A का माप ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"50°"},"2":{"en":"45°"},"3":{"en":"55°"},"4":{"en":"60°"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"256\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 256 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M94 26L26 196L230 196ZM63 102L155 102M42 196A16 16 0 0 0 32 181\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"91\" y=\"16\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"207\">B</text><text x=\"244\" y=\"206\">C</text><text x=\"53\" y=\"106\">D</text><text x=\"165\" y=\"106\">E</text><text x=\"49\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"11\">75°</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"34\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">AD/AB = AE/AC</text></g></svg><br>\\(AD \\cdot AC = AB \\cdot AE \\Rightarrow \\frac{AD}{AB} = \\frac{AE}{AC}\\) with \\(\\angle A\\) common, so \\(\\triangle ADE \\sim \\triangle ABC\\)<br>Hence \\(\\angle ADE = \\angle ABC = 75°\\)<br>Given \\(\\angle ADE = \\angle ACB + 25° \\Rightarrow \\angle ACB = 50°\\)<br>\\(\\angle A = 180° - 75° - 50° = \\boxed{55°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 55°.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"256\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 256 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M94 26L26 196L230 196ZM63 102L155 102M42 196A16 16 0 0 0 32 181\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"91\" y=\"16\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"207\">B</text><text x=\"244\" y=\"206\">C</text><text x=\"53\" y=\"106\">D</text><text x=\"165\" y=\"106\">E</text><text x=\"49\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"11\">75°</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"34\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">AD/AB = AE/AC</text></g></svg><br>\\(AD \\cdot AC = AB \\cdot AE \\Rightarrow \\frac{AD}{AB} = \\frac{AE}{AC}\\) और \\(\\angle A\\) उभयनिष्ठ, अतः \\(\\triangle ADE \\sim \\triangle ABC\\)<br>इसलिए \\(\\angle ADE = \\angle ABC = 75°\\)<br>दिया है \\(\\angle ADE = \\angle ACB + 25° \\Rightarrow \\angle ACB = 50°\\)<br>\\(\\angle A = 180° - 75° - 50° = \\boxed{55°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 55° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000074047","section":"MATH","topic":"Percentage","question":{"en":"The manufacturing cost of an electric drone is split between specialized microchips and lightweight composite casing in a 4:1 ratio. Due to supply chain improvements, microchip costs decrease by 15%, while global material shortages cause the composite casing costs to surge by 40%. What is the net percentage change in the total manufacturing cost of the drone? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक इलेक्ट्रिक ड्रोन की निर्माण लागत विशेष माइक्रोचिप्स और हल्के कंपोज़िट केसिंग के बीच 4:1 के अनुपात में विभाजित है। आपूर्ति शृंखला में सुधार से माइक्रोचिप की लागत 15% घट जाती है, जबकि वैश्विक सामग्री की कमी के कारण कंपोज़िट केसिंग की लागत 40% बढ़ जाती है। ड्रोन की कुल निर्माण लागत में शुद्ध प्रतिशत परिवर्तन क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2% increase","hi":"2% वृद्धि"},"2":{"en":"4% decrease","hi":"4% कमी"},"3":{"en":"3% decrease","hi":"3% कमी"},"4":{"en":"6% increase","hi":"6% वृद्धि"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Take chips \\(= 400\\) and casing \\(= 100\\) (total 500)<br>New \\(= 400(0.85) + 100(1.40) = 340 + 140 = 480\\)<br>Change \\(= \\frac{480 - 500}{500} \\times 100 = \\boxed{4\\%\\ \\text{decrease}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 4% decrease.</b>","hi":"माइक्रोचिप \\(= 400\\) और केसिंग \\(= 100\\) (कुल 500) लीजिए<br>नया \\(= 400(0.85) + 100(1.40) = 340 + 140 = 480\\)<br>परिवर्तन \\(= \\frac{480 - 500}{500} \\times 100 = \\boxed{4\\%\\ \\text{कमी}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 4% कमी है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000074048","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"In a school internal examination of six different subjects, Nishtha scores 64% of the total marks. Nishtha's marks in each subject (separately) are in the ratio 6 : 7 : 9 : 12 : 8 : 6. The maximum marks possible in each subject is the same. As per the rules of the examination, one needs to score 55% in any subject to pass in that subject. In how many subjects in this examination has Nishtha scored below the pass marks? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"छह अलग-अलग विषयों की स्कूल आंतरिक परीक्षा में निष्ठा कुल अंकों का 64% प्राप्त करती है। निष्ठा के प्रत्येक विषय (अलग-अलग) के अंक 6 : 7 : 9 : 12 : 8 : 6 के अनुपात में हैं। प्रत्येक विषय में अधिकतम अंक समान हैं। परीक्षा के नियमानुसार किसी विषय में उत्तीर्ण होने के लिए 55% अंक चाहिए। इस परीक्षा में निष्ठा कितने विषयों में उत्तीर्णांक से कम अंक प्राप्त की है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Total parts \\(= 6 + 7 + 9 + 12 + 8 + 6 = 48\\)<br>These equal 64% of 6M \\(= 3.84M \\Rightarrow\\) 1 part \\(= 0.08M\\)<br>Pass marks \\(= 0.55M \\Rightarrow \\frac{0.55}{0.08} = 6.875\\) parts<br>Subjects with parts below 6.875: 6 and 6 → \\(\\boxed{2}\\) subjects<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 2.</b>","hi":"कुल भाग \\(= 6 + 7 + 9 + 12 + 8 + 6 = 48\\)<br>ये 6M के 64% \\(= 3.84M\\) के बराबर हैं \\(\\Rightarrow\\) 1 भाग \\(= 0.08M\\)<br>उत्तीर्णांक \\(= 0.55M \\Rightarrow \\frac{0.55}{0.08} = 6.875\\) भाग<br>6.875 से कम भाग वाले विषय: 6 और 6 → \\(\\boxed{2}\\) विषय<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000074049","section":"MATH","topic":"Pipe and Cistern","question":{"en":"A cistern has three taps M, N and P, through which water can be taken out from it. Tap M can fill 6 buckets in 30 minutes, tap N can fill 8 buckets in 1 hour 4 minutes and tap P can fill 2 buckets in 20 minutes. When the cistern is filled upto 4/5th of its capacity, all the three taps are opened together, as a result of which the cistern gets emptied in 2 hours 40 minutes. What is the capacity of the cistern if each bucket is identical and can hold 8 liters of water (assuming there is no wastage of water)? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक टंकी में तीन नल M, N और P हैं जिनसे पानी निकाला जा सकता है। नल M, 30 मिनट में 6 बाल्टियाँ भर सकता है, नल N, 1 घंटे 4 मिनट में 8 बाल्टियाँ और नल P, 20 मिनट में 2 बाल्टियाँ भर सकता है। जब टंकी अपनी क्षमता के 4/5 भाग तक भरी हो, तो तीनों नल एक साथ खोल दिए जाते हैं, जिससे टंकी 2 घंटे 40 मिनट में खाली हो जाती है। यदि प्रत्येक बाल्टी समान है और 8 लीटर पानी रख सकती है, तो टंकी की क्षमता क्या है (पानी की कोई बर्बादी नहीं)? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"720 Lts","hi":"720 लीटर"},"2":{"en":"680 Lts","hi":"680 लीटर"},"3":{"en":"650 Lts","hi":"650 लीटर"},"4":{"en":"544 Lts","hi":"544 लीटर"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Rates: M \\(= \\frac{6}{30} = 0.2\\) b/min, N \\(= \\frac{8}{64} = 0.125\\) b/min, P \\(= \\frac{2}{20} = 0.1\\) b/min<br>Together \\(= 0.425\\) buckets/min; in 160 min \\(= 68\\) buckets<br>\\(\\frac{4}{5}C = 68 \\Rightarrow C = 85\\) buckets<br>Capacity \\(= 85 \\times 8 = \\boxed{680\\ \\text{Lts}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 680 Lts.</b>","hi":"दरें: M \\(= \\frac{6}{30} = 0.2\\) बाल्टी/मिनट, N \\(= \\frac{8}{64} = 0.125\\), P \\(= \\frac{2}{20} = 0.1\\)<br>मिलकर \\(= 0.425\\) बाल्टी/मिनट; 160 मिनट में \\(= 68\\) बाल्टी<br>\\(\\frac{4}{5}C = 68 \\Rightarrow C = 85\\) बाल्टी<br>क्षमता \\(= 85 \\times 8 = \\boxed{680\\ \\text{लीटर}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 680 लीटर है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000074050","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"In a right triangle ABC with ∠B = 90°, sin²A + sin²C = ? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"समकोण त्रिभुज ABC में, जहाँ ∠B = 90° है, sin²A + sin²C = ? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"0"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"sin²A"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(A + C = 90° \\Rightarrow C = 90° - A\\), so \\(\\sin C = \\cos A\\)<br>\\(\\sin^2A + \\sin^2C = \\sin^2A + \\cos^2A\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1.</b>","hi":"\\(A + C = 90° \\Rightarrow C = 90° - A\\), अतः \\(\\sin C = \\cos A\\)<br>\\(\\sin^2A + \\sin^2C = \\sin^2A + \\cos^2A\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000074051","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Solve for acute θ: sin(θ + 15°) = cos(θ − 15°) [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"न्यून θ के लिए हल कीजिए: sin(θ + 15°) = cos(θ − 15°) [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"90°"},"2":{"en":"30°"},"3":{"en":"60°"},"4":{"en":"45°"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sin(\\theta + 15°) = \\cos(\\theta - 15°) = \\sin(90° - \\theta + 15°)\\)<br>\\(\\theta + 15° = 105° - \\theta \\Rightarrow 2\\theta = 90°\\)<br>\\(\\theta = \\boxed{45°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 45°.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sin(\\theta + 15°) = \\cos(\\theta - 15°) = \\sin(90° - \\theta + 15°)\\)<br>\\(\\theta + 15° = 105° - \\theta \\Rightarrow 2\\theta = 90°\\)<br>\\(\\theta = \\boxed{45°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 45° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000074052","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If a + b + c = 31 and ab + bc + ca = 37, find the value of a² + b² + c². [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि a + b + c = 31 और ab + bc + ca = 37 है, तो a² + b² + c² का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"961"},"2":{"en":"1035"},"3":{"en":"887"},"4":{"en":"878"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(a^2 + b^2 + c^2 = (a + b + c)^2 - 2(ab + bc + ca)\\)<br>\\(= 961 - 74\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{887}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 887.</b>","hi":"\\(a^2 + b^2 + c^2 = (a + b + c)^2 - 2(ab + bc + ca)\\)<br>\\(= 961 - 74\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{887}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 887 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000074053","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = 6\\), then find the value of \\(x^6 + \\frac{1}{x^6}\\). [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = 6\\) है, तो \\(x^6 + \\frac{1}{x^6}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"39204"},"2":{"en":"39202"},"3":{"en":"39304"},"4":{"en":"39302"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 36 - 2 = 34\\)<br>\\(x^3 + \\frac{1}{x^3} = 6^3 - 3(6) = 216 - 18 = 198\\)<br>\\(x^6 + \\frac{1}{x^6} = 198^2 - 2 = 39204 - 2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{39202}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 39202.</b>","hi":"\\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 36 - 2 = 34\\)<br>\\(x^3 + \\frac{1}{x^3} = 6^3 - 3(6) = 216 - 18 = 198\\)<br>\\(x^6 + \\frac{1}{x^6} = 198^2 - 2 = 39204 - 2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{39202}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 39202 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000074054","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"A vessel contains 240 litres of a mixture of milk and water in the ratio 7:5. First, 40 litres of the mixture are removed and replaced with an equal volume of pure water. Then, 60 litres of the resulting mixture are removed and replaced with an equal volume of pure milk. Find the final ratio of milk to water in the vessel. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक बर्तन में 240 लीटर दूध और पानी का मिश्रण 7:5 के अनुपात में है। पहले 40 लीटर मिश्रण निकालकर उतने ही आयतन के शुद्ध पानी से बदला जाता है। फिर, परिणामी मिश्रण के 60 लीटर निकालकर उतने ही आयतन के शुद्ध दूध से बदला जाता है। बर्तन में दूध और पानी का अंतिम अनुपात ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"62 : 41"},"2":{"en":"21 : 17"},"3":{"en":"97 : 83"},"4":{"en":"59 : 37"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Initially milk \\(= 140\\) L, water \\(= 100\\) L<br>Removing 40 L removes \\(\\frac{7}{12}\\times40 = 23.33\\) L milk and 16.67 L water; adding 40 L water → milk 116.67, water 123.33<br>Removing 60 L removes 29.17 L milk and 30.83 L water; adding 60 L milk → milk 147.5, water 92.5<br>Ratio \\(= \\frac{147.5}{92.5} = \\boxed{59 : 37}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 59 : 37.</b>","hi":"प्रारंभ में दूध \\(= 140\\) लीटर, पानी \\(= 100\\) लीटर<br>40 लीटर निकालने पर \\(\\frac{7}{12}\\times40 = 23.33\\) लीटर दूध और 16.67 लीटर पानी; 40 लीटर पानी मिलाने पर दूध 116.67, पानी 123.33<br>60 लीटर निकालने पर 29.17 लीटर दूध, 30.83 लीटर पानी; 60 लीटर दूध मिलाने पर दूध 147.5, पानी 92.5<br>अनुपात \\(= \\frac{147.5}{92.5} = \\boxed{59 : 37}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 59 : 37 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000074055","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Three circles with non-collinear centers lie in a plane such that each circle touches the other two externally. How many common tangents can be drawn that touch at least two of these circles simultaneously? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"तीन वृत्त जिनके केंद्र संरेख नहीं हैं, एक तल में इस प्रकार स्थित हैं कि प्रत्येक वृत्त अन्य दो को बाह्य रूप से स्पर्श करता है। ऐसी कितनी उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाएँ खींची जा सकती हैं जो कम से कम दो वृत्तों को एक साथ स्पर्श करें? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"9"},"2":{"en":"3"},"3":{"en":"12"},"4":{"en":"6"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Each pair of circles touches externally, so a pair has 3 common tangents (2 direct + 1 transverse)<br>Number of pairs \\(= \\binom{3}{2} = 3\\)<br>Total tangents \\(= 3 \\times 3 = \\boxed{9}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 9.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक युग्म बाह्य रूप से स्पर्श करता है, अतः एक युग्म पर 3 उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाएँ हैं (2 सीधी + 1 तिर्यक)<br>युग्मों की संख्या \\(= \\binom{3}{2} = 3\\)<br>कुल स्पर्श रेखाएँ \\(= 3 \\times 3 = \\boxed{9}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 9 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000074056","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the appropriate preposition.<br>The professor spoke ___ length about the implications of the study. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"in"},"2":{"en":"on"},"3":{"en":"by"},"4":{"en":"at"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “At length” is a fixed phrase meaning in detail or for a long time.</b><br>Completed sentence: “The professor spoke <b>at</b> length about the implications of the study.”<br>“In length” refers to measurement, while “on length” and “by length” are not idiomatic in this context.<br>The intended meaning is a detailed discussion.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): at.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000074057","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Complete the following sentence in indirect speech with the correct option.<br>She said, “I will open the window.”<br>She said that she ___ open the window. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"will"},"2":{"en":"shall"},"3":{"en":"would"},"4":{"en":"can"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: In reported speech, “will” normally changes to “would” after a past reporting verb.</b><br>“Said” is past tense, so the backshift gives “would.”<br>Completed sentence: “She said that she <b>would</b> open the window.”<br>“Will” and “shall” are not backshifted; “can” changes the meaning to ability.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): would.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000074058","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br>Amid the rising threat of state-sponsored cyberattacks,<br>P. while also collaborating with private sector firms to safeguard national digital assets<br>Q. targeting critical infrastructure such as power grids, financial institutions, and defense systems,<br>R. by investing heavily in advanced threat detection and response mechanisms,<br>S. governments worldwide bolstered their cybersecurity frameworks, [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"SPQR"},"2":{"en":"RSPQ"},"3":{"en":"PRQS"},"4":{"en":"SQRP"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: SQRP</b><br>Q describes what the cyberattacks target and completes the opening phrase.<br>S then supplies the main clause: “governments worldwide bolstered their cybersecurity frameworks.”<br>R explains how they did so, and P adds the parallel action of collaboration.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): SQRP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000074059","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"To be successful in today’s world, you require the gift of the gab.<br>What does “the gift of the gab” mean? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The ability to speak fluently and persuasively"},"2":{"en":"The habit of talking too much without making sense"},"3":{"en":"A natural talent for writing poems and stories"},"4":{"en":"The ability to stay silent and observe carefully"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>The gift of the gab (वाक्पटुता) = the ability to speak easily, fluently and persuasively.</b><br>Example: “A good salesperson often has the gift of the gab.”<br>Talking nonsense is not persuasive speech; the idiom concerns speaking, not writing poetry.<br>Staying silent is contrary to its meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The ability to speak fluently and persuasively.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000074060","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the error in the sentence.<br>He speaks too much fast for me to understand. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"understand"},"2":{"en":"fast"},"3":{"en":"much"},"4":{"en":"speaks"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Too” directly modifies the adverb “fast”; “much” is redundant.</b><br>The erroneous part is “much.”<br>Correct sentence: “He speaks too <b>fast</b> for me to understand.”<br>“Speaks,” “fast” and “understand” are all grammatically appropriate in the corrected structure.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): much.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000074061","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the error in the sentence.<br>A Mount Everest is the highest peak in the world. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A"},"2":{"en":"Everest"},"3":{"en":"highest"},"4":{"en":"world"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: No indefinite article is used before the proper name of a mountain.</b><br>“Mount Everest” is a proper noun, so the initial “A” is incorrect.<br>Correct sentence: “<b>Mount Everest</b> is the highest peak in the world.”<br>“Everest,” the superlative “highest” and “world” are correctly used.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): A.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000074062","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br>The constitutional amendment<br>P. to ensure greater fiscal transparency,<br>Q. was introduced in the parliament<br>R. with provisions mandating periodic audits<br>S. of government expenditure across all departments [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"SRPQ"},"2":{"en":"QPRS"},"3":{"en":"PSQR"},"4":{"en":"RQPS"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QPRS</b><br>Q supplies the main predicate: “was introduced in the parliament.”<br>P states the purpose “to ensure greater fiscal transparency.”<br>R introduces mandatory periodic audits, and S specifies that these audits concern government expenditure.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): QPRS.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000074063","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct idiom for the word highlighted in bold.<br>“Benjamin isn't happy now that he's working the <b>graveyard shift</b>.” [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"He is working at a cemetery."},"2":{"en":"He is working late-night hours."},"3":{"en":"He is working fewer hours than before."},"4":{"en":"He is working in a dangerous job."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Graveyard shift (रात्रि पाली) = a work shift during the late night, usually ending early in the morning.</b><br>Example: “Nurses often work the graveyard shift.”<br>The expression does not literally mean working in a cemetery.<br>It specifies night hours, not fewer hours or occupational danger.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): He is working late-night hours.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000074064","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?<br>1. Over generations, cultural and genetic adaptations improved their resilience to extreme environments.<br>2. They created insulated clothing from animal skins and built durable shelters to retain heat.<br>3. Early humans living during the Ice Age had to develop survival strategies to endure harsh conditions.<br>4. The ability to control fire allowed them to cook food, stay warm, and protect themselves from predators.<br>5. These adaptations enabled human populations to spread across colder regions and establish new settlements. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5-2-3-1-4"},"2":{"en":"1-3-2-4-5"},"3":{"en":"4-1-2-5-3"},"4":{"en":"3-2-4-5-1"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 3-2-4-5-1</b><br>Sentence 3 introduces early humans and their need for survival strategies.<br>Sentences 2 and 4 describe those strategies: clothing, shelters and fire; sentence 5 states their result.<br>Sentence 1 then extends the account to adaptations over generations.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 3-2-4-5-1.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000074065","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?<br>1. Mass media plays a crucial role in shaping public opinion and cultural norms.<br>2. Understanding media literacy is essential to critically analyze and interpret information.<br>3. The influence of media extends to politics, social behavior, and consumer choices.<br>4. While it can educate and inform, media can also spread misinformation and biases. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4-3-2-1"},"2":{"en":"1-3-4-2"},"3":{"en":"3-2-1-4"},"4":{"en":"2-4-1-3"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 1-3-4-2</b><br>Sentence 1 introduces media’s broad influence, and sentence 3 gives specific domains.<br>Sentence 4 presents its beneficial and harmful sides.<br>Sentence 2 concludes with the need for media literacy to evaluate information critically.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1-3-4-2.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000074066","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: <b>PERNICIOUS</b> [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Harmless"},"2":{"en":"Deadly"},"3":{"en":"Helpful"},"4":{"en":"Safe"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Pernicious (घातक, हानिकारक) = having a very harmful or deadly effect.</b><br><b>Harmless (अहानिकारक)</b> = not causing harm<br><b>Deadly (घातक)</b> = causing or capable of causing death ✔<br><b>Helpful (सहायक)</b> = useful or beneficial<br><b>Safe (सुरक्षित)</b> = free from danger<br>More synonyms: destructive, noxious, lethal.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Deadly.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000074067","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the given passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage intently and choose the most appropriate option to fill in each blank:<br><br>To regard competitive examinations as neutral arbiters of merit is to mistake calibration for fairness. These trials, draped in metrics and flanked by syllabi, often merely echo the (1)___ of systemic inequities rather than resolving them. What appears to be an open arena is, upon closer scrutiny, a scaffolded labyrinth—its paths more navigable to the already initiated. In this theatre, memory masquerades as intellect, and swiftness is crowned over (2) ___. Coaching bazaars thrive, not on illumination but on algorithmic mimicry. One does not so much learn as rehearse patterned responses, choreographed to match opaque rubrics. That which resists formula—intuition, ambiguity, ethical judgment—is too often filtered out as noise. Yet the deeper toll is not pedagogical but psychic. Prolonged exposure to anticipatory failure creates a cognitive sediment, an internalized narrowing. Dreams don’t shatter; they (3)___, calcifying into compliance. In time, the examinee becomes fluent in performance, but foreign to inquiry. To call for reform is insufficient. We must interrogate the architecture itself—its values, its exclusions, its gods. Until the grammar of merit is (4)___, not rebranded, no revision will suffice. The danger is not that we aim too high, but that the scaffolding remains unseen, and the climb is mistaken for (5)___.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number (1)? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"legacies"},"2":{"en":"ruptures"},"3":{"en":"inversions"},"4":{"en":"echoes"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Legacies (विरासत, परिणाम) = long-lasting results of past events.</b><br>Examinations reproduce the enduring legacies of systemic inequities rather than resolving them.<br><b>Ruptures (विभाजन)</b> = breaks or breaches<br><b>Inversions (उलटफेर)</b> = reversals; <b>echoes (प्रतिध्वनि)</b> repeats the verb and is illogical as the object of “echo.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): legacies.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000074068","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the given passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage intently and choose the most appropriate option to fill in each blank:<br><br>To regard competitive examinations as neutral arbiters of merit is to mistake calibration for fairness. These trials, draped in metrics and flanked by syllabi, often merely echo the (1)___ of systemic inequities rather than resolving them. What appears to be an open arena is, upon closer scrutiny, a scaffolded labyrinth—its paths more navigable to the already initiated. In this theatre, memory masquerades as intellect, and swiftness is crowned over (2) ___. Coaching bazaars thrive, not on illumination but on algorithmic mimicry. One does not so much learn as rehearse patterned responses, choreographed to match opaque rubrics. That which resists formula—intuition, ambiguity, ethical judgment—is too often filtered out as noise. Yet the deeper toll is not pedagogical but psychic. Prolonged exposure to anticipatory failure creates a cognitive sediment, an internalized narrowing. Dreams don’t shatter; they (3)___, calcifying into compliance. In time, the examinee becomes fluent in performance, but foreign to inquiry. To call for reform is insufficient. We must interrogate the architecture itself—its values, its exclusions, its gods. Until the grammar of merit is (4)___, not rebranded, no revision will suffice. The danger is not that we aim too high, but that the scaffolding remains unseen, and the climb is mistaken for (5)___.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number (2)? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"urgency"},"2":{"en":"depth"},"3":{"en":"compliance"},"4":{"en":"abstraction"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Depth (गहराई) = profound thought or understanding.</b><br>The passage contrasts superficial speed with intellectual depth: “swiftness is crowned over depth.”<br><b>Urgency (तात्कालिकता)</b> = pressing haste<br><b>Compliance (अनुपालन)</b> = conformity; <b>abstraction (अमूर्तता)</b> = an idea without concrete detail<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): depth.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000074069","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the given passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage intently and choose the most appropriate option to fill in each blank:<br><br>To regard competitive examinations as neutral arbiters of merit is to mistake calibration for fairness. These trials, draped in metrics and flanked by syllabi, often merely echo the (1)___ of systemic inequities rather than resolving them. What appears to be an open arena is, upon closer scrutiny, a scaffolded labyrinth—its paths more navigable to the already initiated. In this theatre, memory masquerades as intellect, and swiftness is crowned over (2) ___. Coaching bazaars thrive, not on illumination but on algorithmic mimicry. One does not so much learn as rehearse patterned responses, choreographed to match opaque rubrics. That which resists formula—intuition, ambiguity, ethical judgment—is too often filtered out as noise. Yet the deeper toll is not pedagogical but psychic. Prolonged exposure to anticipatory failure creates a cognitive sediment, an internalized narrowing. Dreams don’t shatter; they (3)___, calcifying into compliance. In time, the examinee becomes fluent in performance, but foreign to inquiry. To call for reform is insufficient. We must interrogate the architecture itself—its values, its exclusions, its gods. Until the grammar of merit is (4)___, not rebranded, no revision will suffice. The danger is not that we aim too high, but that the scaffolding remains unseen, and the climb is mistaken for (5)___.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number (3)? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"intensify"},"2":{"en":"dissolve"},"3":{"en":"fossilize"},"4":{"en":"scatter"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Fossilize (जमकर स्थिर हो जाना) = become rigid and incapable of change.</b><br>It fits “calcifying into compliance”: dreams harden and lose vitality rather than shatter.<br><b>Intensify (तीव्र होना)</b> = become stronger<br><b>Dissolve (घुलना)</b> = disappear into liquid; <b>scatter (बिखरना)</b> = disperse in different directions<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): fossilize.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000074070","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the given passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage intently and choose the most appropriate option to fill in each blank:<br><br>To regard competitive examinations as neutral arbiters of merit is to mistake calibration for fairness. These trials, draped in metrics and flanked by syllabi, often merely echo the (1)___ of systemic inequities rather than resolving them. What appears to be an open arena is, upon closer scrutiny, a scaffolded labyrinth—its paths more navigable to the already initiated. In this theatre, memory masquerades as intellect, and swiftness is crowned over (2) ___. Coaching bazaars thrive, not on illumination but on algorithmic mimicry. One does not so much learn as rehearse patterned responses, choreographed to match opaque rubrics. That which resists formula—intuition, ambiguity, ethical judgment—is too often filtered out as noise. Yet the deeper toll is not pedagogical but psychic. Prolonged exposure to anticipatory failure creates a cognitive sediment, an internalized narrowing. Dreams don’t shatter; they (3)___, calcifying into compliance. In time, the examinee becomes fluent in performance, but foreign to inquiry. To call for reform is insufficient. We must interrogate the architecture itself—its values, its exclusions, its gods. Until the grammar of merit is (4)___, not rebranded, no revision will suffice. The danger is not that we aim too high, but that the scaffolding remains unseen, and the climb is mistaken for (5)___.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number (4)? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"unlearned"},"2":{"en":"dismantled"},"3":{"en":"alphabetized"},"4":{"en":"glorified"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Dismantled (ध्वस्त किया गया) = taken apart or abolished.</b><br>The author argues that the entire architecture of merit must be dismantled, not merely rebranded.<br><b>Unlearned (भुला दिया गया)</b> = deliberately forgotten<br><b>Alphabetized (वर्णक्रम में रखा गया)</b> = arranged alphabetically; <b>glorified (महिमामंडित)</b> = praised excessively<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): dismantled.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000074071","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the given passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage intently and choose the most appropriate option to fill in each blank:<br><br>To regard competitive examinations as neutral arbiters of merit is to mistake calibration for fairness. These trials, draped in metrics and flanked by syllabi, often merely echo the (1)___ of systemic inequities rather than resolving them. What appears to be an open arena is, upon closer scrutiny, a scaffolded labyrinth—its paths more navigable to the already initiated. In this theatre, memory masquerades as intellect, and swiftness is crowned over (2) ___. Coaching bazaars thrive, not on illumination but on algorithmic mimicry. One does not so much learn as rehearse patterned responses, choreographed to match opaque rubrics. That which resists formula—intuition, ambiguity, ethical judgment—is too often filtered out as noise. Yet the deeper toll is not pedagogical but psychic. Prolonged exposure to anticipatory failure creates a cognitive sediment, an internalized narrowing. Dreams don’t shatter; they (3)___, calcifying into compliance. In time, the examinee becomes fluent in performance, but foreign to inquiry. To call for reform is insufficient. We must interrogate the architecture itself—its values, its exclusions, its gods. Until the grammar of merit is (4)___, not rebranded, no revision will suffice. The danger is not that we aim too high, but that the scaffolding remains unseen, and the climb is mistaken for (5)___.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number (5)? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"progress"},"2":{"en":"destination"},"3":{"en":"transformation"},"4":{"en":"justice"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Progress (प्रगति) = advancement towards a better state.</b><br>The unseen scaffolding makes people mistake the act of climbing the system for genuine progress.<br><b>Destination (गंतव्य)</b> = the place being reached; a climb cannot literally be a destination.<br><b>Transformation (रूपांतरण)</b> = complete change; <b>justice (न्याय)</b> = fairness<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): progress.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000074072","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Select the correct option:<br>No matter how ___ the evidence was, the jury remained unconvinced. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"compelling"},"2":{"en":"compel"},"3":{"en":"compels"},"4":{"en":"compulsion"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The structure “how + adjective + subject + be” requires an adjective.</b><br>“Compelling” means powerfully convincing (दमदार, सम्मोहक).<br>Completed sentence: “No matter how <b>compelling</b> the evidence was, the jury remained unconvinced.”<br>“Compel” and “compels” are verbs; “compulsion” is a noun meaning forced pressure.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): compelling.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000074073","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>People have elected her president. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She has elected president by people."},"2":{"en":"She has been elected president."},"3":{"en":"She was elected president."},"4":{"en":"She is being elected president."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Present perfect passive = has/have been + past participle.</b><br>“Her” becomes “she,” and the complement “president” remains.<br>Correct form: “She <b>has been elected</b> president.”<br>Option 1 omits the passive auxiliary; option 3 changes to simple past; option 4 changes to present continuous.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): She has been elected president.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000074074","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>The clerk has been processing the applications. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The applications have processed by the clerk."},"2":{"en":"The applications have been being processed by the clerk."},"3":{"en":"The applications are being processed by the clerk."},"4":{"en":"The applications have been processed by the clerk."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Present perfect continuous passive = has/have been being + past participle.</b><br>The plural object “the applications” becomes the subject and takes “have.”<br>Correct form: “The applications <b>have been being processed</b> by the clerk.”<br>Option 1 omits “been being”; option 3 changes the tense; option 4 uses present perfect passive, not continuous.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The applications have been being processed by the clerk.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000074075","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Convert the sentence provided below from its passive voice structure to an active voice structure:<br>Was the report being edited by the communications team when you checked? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Was the communications team editing the report when you checked?"},"2":{"en":"Did the team edit the report you checked?"},"3":{"en":"Were you checking the report while it was edited?"},"4":{"en":"The report was being edited after you checked."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Past continuous passive questions change to “Was/Were + agent + verb-ing + object?”</b><br>The agent “the communications team” becomes the subject.<br>Correct form: “<b>Was the communications team editing</b> the report when you checked?”<br>B changes tense and structure; C changes the agent and focus; D remains passive and changes the time relation.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Was the communications team editing the report when you checked?.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000074076","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Convert the sentence provided below from its passive voice structure to an active voice structure:<br>The changes were not anticipated to have created such widespread confusion. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"No one had anticipated the changes to create such confusion."},"2":{"en":"The confusion anticipated change wasn't widespread."},"3":{"en":"It wasn’t anticipated that changes caused confusion."},"4":{"en":"Changes were confused before they were anticipated."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: An unspecified agent in a passive construction can be expressed as “no one.”</b><br>The negative passive “were not anticipated” becomes “No one had anticipated,” with the changes as the object.<br>B and D distort the meaning and relationships.<br>C remains impersonal and changes the aspect, whereas A gives the direct active construction.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): No one had anticipated the changes to create such confusion.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000074077","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence:<br>The boy <b>fell down from</b> the bicycle. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"fell down of"},"2":{"en":"fell off"},"3":{"en":"fell from"},"4":{"en":"dropped off"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Fall off” is the standard phrasal verb for accidentally dropping from a vehicle or surface.</b><br>Correct sentence: “The boy <b>fell off</b> the bicycle.”<br>“Fell down of” is unidiomatic; “fell from” is possible but less natural for a bicycle accident.<br>“Dropped off” means fell asleep, decreased, or delivered someone, so it does not fit.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): fell off.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000074078","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in direct speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding indirect speech.<br>She said to him, “Are you coming to the party?” [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She asked him was he coming to the party."},"2":{"en":"She asked him if he is coming to the party."},"3":{"en":"She asked him if he was coming to the party."},"4":{"en":"She asked him are you coming to the party."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Report yes/no questions with “if/whether,” statement word order and backshifted tense.</b><br>“Are you coming” becomes “if he was coming.”<br>A uses question inversion and omits “if”; B fails to backshift “is.”<br>D retains direct question order and the second-person pronoun.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): She asked him if he was coming to the party.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000074079","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech.<br>The teacher informed the students that the results would be declared the following Monday. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"“The results will be declared next Monday,” the teacher said."},"2":{"en":"“We declare the results next Monday,” the teacher said."},"3":{"en":"“The results would be declared next Monday,” the teacher said."},"4":{"en":"“Your results are going to be declared on Monday,” said the teacher."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Would” returns to “will,” and “the following Monday” returns to “next Monday.”</b><br>The passive future construction remains “will be declared.”<br>B changes the voice and omits the future marker.<br>C retains “would”; D changes the time reference and future construction.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): “The results will be declared next Monday,” the teacher said.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000074080","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech.<br>He said that he would prefer to remain silent rather than speak without proof. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"“I would prefer to stay silent than speak without proof,” he said."},"2":{"en":"“I prefer silence over false claims,” he said."},"3":{"en":"“I'd rather not talk if there's no proof,” said he."},"4":{"en":"“I would prefer to remain silent rather than speak without proof,” he said."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Change the reported third-person pronoun to the speaker’s first person while retaining the stated preference.</b><br>“He would prefer” becomes “I would prefer,” and “rather than” remains unchanged.<br>A omits “rather”; B and C paraphrase the sentence and alter its wording and degree of certainty.<br>D preserves the exact meaning and structure.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): “I would prefer to remain silent rather than speak without proof,” he said.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};